flow Saturday Night and Sunday, with a lull Sunday Night, then occasionally again in the south-southeast flow along and just in advance of a heavy line of showers and thunderstorms on Monday Morning. The onshore flow, and to a lesser extent the heavy rainfall, lead to multiple rounds of coastal flooding along the oceanfront and back bays with the high tide cycles on Sunday evening and again on Monday Morning.', 'The Passaic River at Pine Brook rose above flood stage of 19.0 feet to a maximum of 19.24 feet.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (778488, 201809, 3, 1630, 201809, 3, 1638, 129951, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '03-SEP-18 16:30:00', 'EST-5', '03-SEP-18 16:38:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '25.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'CHURCHILL', 0, 'N', 'CHURCHILL', 41.17, -80.67, 41.17, -80.67, 'A cold front moved across the region on September 3rd causing scattered showers and thunderstorms to form.  A couple of thunderstorms became severe and produced some minor damage.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed several trees across Liberty Township.  A house was damaged by a fallen tree on 5th Avenue.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (794843, 201811, 13, 447, 201811, 13, 447, 132836, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'November', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'MHX', '13-NOV-18 04:47:00', 'EST-5', '13-NOV-18 04:47:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 50, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'WNW', 'MOREHEAD CITY', 0, 'WNW', 'MOREHEAD CITY', 34.7215, -76.7059, 34.7215, -76.7059, 'A supercell thunderstorm came ashore across Carteret County and produced a variety of severe weather. A waterspout formed offshore and came on land as a tornado. Severe thunderstorm winds also occurred in association with the same storm. Another severe thunderstorm produced wind damage in Beaufort County.', 'Personal weather station measured a 58 MPH gust at the Morehead City Yacht Basin.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (746471, 201804, 17, 2000, 201804, 17, 2345, 123555, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'April', 'Flood', 'PHI', '17-APR-18 20:00:00', 'EST-5', '17-APR-18 23:45:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'NE', 'OUTCALT', 1, 'NE', 'OUTCALT', 40.3894, -74.3906, 40.3892, -74.39, 'A strong backdoor cold front moved from northeast to southwest across the area late Saturday afternoon April 15th into Sunday morning April 16th. Not only was there a significant drop in temperature coinciding with the passage of the front, but also a stark difference between high temperatures on Saturday and Sunday. On Saturday, high temperatures ranged from the mid-70s to mid-80s, but only made it to the mid-30s to mid-40s on Sunday. In general, there was a 40 degree temperature drop from Saturday to Sunday! ||The backdoor front became stationary south of the region then moved northward as a warm front Sunday night into Monday morning. Meanwhile, a strong cold front approached from the west and swept across the area Monday afternoon and evening, along with an attendant area of low pressure. This robust storm system tapped large amounts of moisture, which was lifted along the warm front as overrunning precipitation, and along the cold front as a line of showers and thunderstorms. ||As a result, heavy rainfall occurred across the region. A widespread 1 to 3 inches of rainfall occurred, with localized amounts over 4 inches, especially across the northern half of New Jersey. As a result, flooding occurred across portions of the area. Meanwhile, it was cold enough in the higher elevations of Sussex County New Jersey for freezing rain on Sunday.||Along the coast, an extended period of onshore flow occurred, beginning with east-northeast winds Saturday Night, which then shifted to the southeast on Sunday Night into Monday Morning April 16th. Widespread winds gusts of 40 to 50 mph occurred in the east-northeast flow Saturday Night and Sunday, with a lull Sunday Night, then occasionally again in the south-southeast flow along and just in advance of a heavy line of showers and thunderstorms on Monday Morning. The onshore flow, and to a lesser extent the heavy rainfall, lead to multiple rounds of coastal flooding along the oceanfront and back bays with the high tide cycles on Sunday evening and again on Monday Morning.', 'The Manalapan Brook at Spotswood rose to flood stage at 19 feet, reaching a maximum of  19.02 feet.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (743412, 201803, 19, 1643, 201803, 19, 1653, 123500, 'GEORGIA', 13, 2018, 'March', 'Hail', 'FFC', '19-MAR-18 16:43:00', 'EST-5', '19-MAR-18 16:53:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '40.00K', NULL, 'Broadcast Media', 1.75, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, 'E', 'DRAYTON', 4, 'E', 'DRAYTON', 32.0796, -83.8796, 32.0796, -83.8796, 'Widespread severe thunderstorms broke out across central and north Georgia during the evening hours of March 19th, through the early morning hours of the 20th as a warm front lifted north across the region ahead of a strong storm system developing across the lower Mississippi Valley.', 'Broadcast media reported golf ball sized hail along Tiger Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (774606, 201809, 10, 2159, 201809, 10, 2220, 129275, 'SOUTH CAROLINA', 45, 2018, 'September', 'Flash Flood', 'CAE', '10-SEP-18 21:59:00', 'EST-5', '10-SEP-18 22:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.10K', '0.10K', 'Law Enforcement', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'ENE', 'GRANITEVILLE', 0, 'S', 'WARRENVILLE', 33.5732, -81.8133, 33.545, -81.8195, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed in a moist and unstable environment, some of which reached severe limits and produced wind damage, and some that produced locally heavy rain and flooding, during the afternoon into the nighttime of Sept 10.', 'Numerous roads were flooded and closed in Graniteville, including Canal St, Ascauga Lake Rd, and Hwy 421. One person was rescued from a car.  Another person was being rescued from a home.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (774607, 201809, 10, 1900, 201809, 10, 2100, 129275, 'SOUTH CAROLINA', 45, 2018, 'September', 'Heavy Rain', 'CAE', '10-SEP-18 19:00:00', 'EST-5', '10-SEP-18 21:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Public', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'NORTH AUGUSTA', 0, 'N', 'NORTH AUGUSTA', 33.5, -81.97, 33.5, -81.97, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed in a moist and unstable environment, some of which reached severe limits and produced wind damage, and some that produced locally heavy rain and flooding, during the afternoon into the nighttime of Sept 10.', 'Public observer measured 2.95 inches of rain as of 2100 EST (2200 EDT) in North Augusta, SC. It is estimated that rain began around 1900 EST (2000 EDT). The final total amount of rain received is unknown.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (780609, 201809, 27, 1818, 201809, 27, 1820, 130401, 'SOUTH CAROLINA', 45, 2018, 'September', 'Hail', 'CAE', '27-SEP-18 18:18:00', 'EST-5', '27-SEP-18 18:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.10K', '0.10K', 'Trained Spotter', 0.25, NULL, NULL, NULL, 6, 'WNW', 'HAMMOND XRDS', 6, 'WNW', 'HAMMOND XRDS', 33.78, -80.97, 33.78, -80.97, 'An approaching cold front, an upper disturbance, and diurnal heating contributed to scattered thunderstorm development in the afternoon and evening, a few of which reached severe limits.', 'SKYWARN spotter reported pea sized hail, lasting a few minutes.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (778486, 201809, 3, 1623, 201809, 3, 1623, 129952, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '03-SEP-18 16:23:00', 'EST-5', '03-SEP-18 16:23:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'EDINBORO', 0, 'N', 'EDINBORO', 41.87, -80.13, 41.87, -80.13, 'A cold front moved across the region on September 3rd causing scattered showers and thunderstorms to form.  A couple of thunderstorms became severe and produced some minor damage.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed a tree.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (794791, 201811, 24, 1406, 201811, 24, 1407, 132837, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'November', 'Tornado', 'MHX', '24-NOV-18 14:06:00', 'EST-5', '24-NOV-18 14:07:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'NWS Storm Survey', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'NNE', 'CAPE CARTERET', 1, 'SSE', 'CEDAR PT', 34.6867, -77.0456, 34.6906, -77.0456, 'A supercell thunderstorm came ashore in Carteret County and produced several tornadoes, as well as severe thunderstorm wind gusts.', 'The tornado path started along the shores of Bogue Sound near Bayshore|Drive in Cape Carteret and quickly moved north-northeast across Live Oak Drive. An|eyewitness here saw the tornado move down the street. Damage included|minor uplift of a porch, along with some siding and a uprooted tree. |More damage occurred along Park Avenue from near Live Oak Drive to Easy|Street. Most of the significant damage was blown toward the north |(southerly wind) and included large limbs down, along with damage to a |power line. In addition some shingles were blown off of a new roof. Of |interest was a tremendous amount of leaf debris that was along the north|and east sides of the houses along both Live Oak Drive and Park Avenue.|Although very subtle, this leaf debris could only occur on those sides |of the homes with a north to northeast wind, which was in the opposite |direction of most of the storm damage and therefore indicated likely |rotation. The damage path ended near the corner of Park Avenue and Easy|Street.||Overall damage along the path was relatively minor with 1 tree uprooted|that was already leaning due to Florence, and minor shingle loss of |another structure. Top winds were estimated to be around 80 mph or an |EF0 tornado.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769765, 201808, 12, 1712, 201808, 12, 1712, 127766, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '12-AUG-18 17:12:00', 'EST-5', '12-AUG-18 17:12:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', '0.00K', 'Utility Company', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'E', 'ROCKWOOD', 1, 'E', 'ROCKWOOD', 39.921, -79.1363, 39.921, -79.1363, 'A few storms developed over the Laurel Highlands during the evening of August 12, 2018 and one storm produced wind damage in Somerset County.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down trees onto wires northeast of Rockwood.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769758, 201808, 8, 1902, 201808, 8, 1902, 127765, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '08-AUG-18 19:02:00', 'EST-5', '08-AUG-18 19:02:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'N', 'ROADSIDE', 1, 'N', 'ROADSIDE', 39.7846, -77.529, 39.7846, -77.529, 'A short line of storms developed over the south-central mountains of Pennsylvania during the early evening hours of August 8, 2018. One storm in this line produced wind damage in Franklin County.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down multiple trees in Quincy Township.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769737, 201808, 7, 1255, 201808, 7, 1255, 127764, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '07-AUG-18 12:55:00', 'EST-5', '07-AUG-18 12:55:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'NNW', 'WEST MILTON', 0, 'NNW', 'WEST MILTON', 41.0231, -76.8818, 41.0231, -76.8818, 'A broken line of storms developed across central Pennsylvania during the afternoon hours of August 7, 2018 in a high CAPE environment as a weak shortwave crossed New England. Several reports of wind damage were received, primarily across the middle and lower Susquehanna Valley.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down trees and wires on Milroy Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769738, 201808, 7, 1346, 201808, 7, 1346, 127764, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '07-AUG-18 13:46:00', 'EST-5', '07-AUG-18 13:46:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'EAST LEWISBURG', 1, 'SE', 'EAST LEWISBURG', 40.9633, -76.8609, 40.9633, -76.8609, 'A broken line of storms developed across central Pennsylvania during the afternoon hours of August 7, 2018 in a high CAPE environment as a weak shortwave crossed New England. Several reports of wind damage were received, primarily across the middle and lower Susquehanna Valley.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down trees and wires on 3rd Street in Montandon.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769745, 201808, 7, 1452, 201808, 7, 1452, 127764, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '07-AUG-18 14:52:00', 'EST-5', '07-AUG-18 14:52:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NE', 'LOCUSTDALE', 1, 'NE', 'LOCUSTDALE', 40.7804, -76.3554, 40.7804, -76.3554, 'A broken line of storms developed across central Pennsylvania during the afternoon hours of August 7, 2018 in a high CAPE environment as a weak shortwave crossed New England. Several reports of wind damage were received, primarily across the middle and lower Susquehanna Valley.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down wires at the intersection of Route 61 and Route 54.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776505, 201807, 16, 1955, 201807, 16, 1955, 129626, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '16-JUL-18 19:55:00', 'EST-5', '16-JUL-18 19:55:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'JAMESTOWN', 1, 'W', 'JAMESTOWN', 42.1, -79.24, 42.1, -79.24, 'A very warm and humid air mass was in place across western and north central New York. As is usually the case with an approaching cold front, thunderstorms fired up along a pre-frontal boundary that extended from the Lake Erie shoreline northeast to Rochester. As the storms grew northeast along this boundary, they eventually encountered an outflow boundary pushing south from Lake Ontario. The intersecting boundaries fueled more impressive storms. Given high precipitable water values, the strong updrafts in these boundary enhanced storms generated copious amounts of lightning. Low topped convection does not allow for such electrification as a deep mixed phase layer is not present. The tight clustering of these lightning cores, when combined with strong divergence at cloud top was enough to generate storms that produced wind damage.', 'Trees down outside Jamestown.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776506, 201807, 16, 2111, 201807, 16, 2111, 129626, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '16-JUL-18 21:11:00', 'EST-5', '16-JUL-18 21:11:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '10.00K', '0.00K', 'Park/Forest Service', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NNW', 'DARIEN CENTER', 1, 'NNW', 'DARIEN CENTER', 42.9123, -78.4085, 42.9123, -78.4085, 'A very warm and humid air mass was in place across western and north central New York. As is usually the case with an approaching cold front, thunderstorms fired up along a pre-frontal boundary that extended from the Lake Erie shoreline northeast to Rochester. As the storms grew northeast along this boundary, they eventually encountered an outflow boundary pushing south from Lake Ontario. The intersecting boundaries fueled more impressive storms. Given high precipitable water values, the strong updrafts in these boundary enhanced storms generated copious amounts of lightning. Low topped convection does not allow for such electrification as a deep mixed phase layer is not present. The tight clustering of these lightning cores, when combined with strong divergence at cloud top was enough to generate storms that produced wind damage.', 'Several trees down with damage to camping equipment at Darien Lakes State Park.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776546, 201807, 28, 615, 201807, 28, 615, 129633, 'LAKE ERIE', 95, 2018, 'July', 'Waterspout', 'BUF', '28-JUL-18 06:15:00', 'EST-5', '28-JUL-18 06:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Social Media', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 43, 'SW', 'BUFFALO HARBOR', 43, 'SW', 'BUFFALO HARBOR', 42.4251, -79.4643, 42.4251, -79.4643, 'A broad closed low located just south of James Bay brought conditions reminiscent of fall across the Lower Great Lakes. The lake to 850 mb temperature difference was about 12C, while thermal profiles showed lake induced equilibrium level heights around 30kft. A weak secondary cold front crossed Lake Erie, constructively working with the land breeze boundary to enhance surface convergence. A lone shower developed along the land breeze boundary just off shore of Portland, NY, around 7 AM. This shower spawned a waterspout.', 'A picture of a waterspout was posted on the Facebook page located off of Portland, NY, with a time of 7:15 AM local.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (789917, 201810, 2, 1558, 201810, 2, 1558, 129857, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'October', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'OKX', '02-OCT-18 15:58:00', 'EST-5', '02-OCT-18 15:58:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '3.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NE', 'MT KISCO', 1, 'NE', 'MT KISCO', 41.2086, -73.7361, 41.2086, -73.7361, 'An approaching cold front triggered severe thunderstorms across southeastern New York, they produced 3 tornadoes across Rockland, Westchester and Suffolk Counties.', 'Trees down on Saw Mill River Parkway and Main Street.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (790149, 201810, 2, 2036, 201810, 2, 2106, 132040, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'October', 'Flash Flood', 'OKX', '02-OCT-18 20:36:00', 'EST-5', '02-OCT-18 21:06:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Amateur Radio', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'NE', 'BLOOMINGDALE', 0, 'NE', 'BLOOMINGDALE', 41.0236, -74.2962, 41.0236, -74.2967, 'A warm front lifted north across the area through the day on October 2nd, leaving the local area in the warm sector. Multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms developed and moved through the region. With wet antecedent conditions from recent rainfall and plenty of available moisture as precipitable water values approached two inches, these showers and storms resulted in flash flooding across portions of northeast New Jersey. Rainfall totals across the region generally ranged from 1-3 inches, with a CoCoRaHS observer in Oakland reporting 2.30 inches.', 'Ringwood Avenue in Wanaque was closed northbound at Whistler Place due to flooding.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (777426, 201807, 16, 1252, 201807, 16, 1252, 129782, 'LAKE HURON', 90, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Hail', 'APX', '16-JUL-18 12:52:00', 'EST-5', '16-JUL-18 12:52:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, 'NE', 'GREENBUSH', 2, 'NE', 'GREENBUSH', 44.5891, -83.3011, 44.5891, -83.3011, 'An organizing line of storms produced significant weather as it moved off of northeast lower Michigan.', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (777427, 201807, 16, 1335, 201807, 16, 1335, 129782, 'LAKE HURON', 90, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'APX', '16-JUL-18 13:35:00', 'EST-5', '16-JUL-18 13:35:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Trained Spotter', 35, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'OSSINEKE', 1, 'ENE', 'OSSINEKE', 44.9278, -83.3984, 44.9278, -83.3984, 'An organizing line of storms produced significant weather as it moved off of northeast lower Michigan.', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755000, 201807, 3, 1738, 201807, 3, 1738, 125935, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 17:38:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 17:38:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'DELAIR', 1, 'SE', 'DELAIR', 39.96, -75.06, 39.96, -75.06, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southwestern New Jersey on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell along the Interstate 95/New Jersey Turnpike Corridor in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'Numerous trees reported down in Pennsauken. Time estimated from radar.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758178, 201807, 20, 1750, 201807, 20, 1750, 126488, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '20-JUL-18 17:50:00', 'EST-5', '20-JUL-18 17:50:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', 'Emergency Manager', 45, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NE', 'BULGER', 1, 'NE', 'BULGER', 38.1462, -81.9649, 38.1462, -81.9649, 'Showers and thunderstorms formed across the middle Ohio River Valley on the 20th as a warm front lifted through. The showers and storms eventually organized into a line which moved through central and southern West Virginia during the early evening. Sub-severe wind gusts caused isolated tree damage, wind observations across the area were generally 35 to 45 knots. One tree was also struck by lightning earlier that afternoon and fell onto a home and car.', 'A tree was blown down across Bark Camp Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760663, 201807, 18, 1315, 201807, 18, 1315, 126911, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '18-JUL-18 13:15:00', 'EST-5', '18-JUL-18 13:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 36, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 6, 'NNW', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 6, 'NNW', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 28.6336, -80.8075, 28.6336, -80.8075, 'A mid-level trough was located near the eastern seaboard with a weak extension into the southeastern states. This kept the Atlantic high pressure ridge suppressed across south Florida and provided low-to-mid level southwest wind flow. Moisture was abundant across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Scattered to numerous showers developed along the west coast sea breeze and pushed across the state through the afternoon. With the stout southwest flow, the east coast sea breeze was pinned along the east coast for most of the day. When the two sea breezes collided near the east coast, the strongest storms developed and pushed east across Brevard County. Several of these storms produced strong wind gusts along the intracoastal waters.', 'Weatherflow site XPAR at Parrish Park near Titusville measured a peak wind gust of 36 knots from the west.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763456, 201807, 22, 1459, 201807, 22, 1459, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 14:59:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 14:59:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 39, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 3, 'WSW', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 3, 'WSW', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 28.36, -80.65, 28.36, -80.65, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'A Weatherflow site on the Banana River just south of State Road 520 on Merritt Island  (XCCB) measured a peak wind gust of 39 knots from the northwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763458, 201807, 22, 1518, 201807, 22, 1518, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 15:18:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 15:18:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'ASOS', 42, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'NNW', 'MELBOURNE', 2, 'NNW', 'MELBOURNE', 28.101, -80.612, 28.101, -80.612, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'The ASOS at the Melbourne International Airport (KMLB) measured a peak wind gust of 42 knots from the north.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (783629, 201809, 6, 1434, 201809, 6, 1434, 130987, 'CONNECTICUT', 9, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '06-SEP-18 14:34:00', 'EST-5', '06-SEP-18 14:34:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'State Official', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SW', 'PLEASANT VLY', 1, 'SW', 'PLEASANT VLY', 41.89, -73.01, 41.89, -73.01, 'A cold front crossed northwest Connecticut on the 6th, bringing and end to a four-day heat wave. This front sparked a broken line of thunderstorms during the afternoon as it interacted with the hot and humid airmass. Some of these storms became severe, resulting in scattered reports of wind damage.', 'A tree was downed onto wires.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771660, 201807, 27, 1241, 201807, 27, 1241, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 12:41:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 12:41:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NE', 'NORTH BETHLEHEM', 1, 'NE', 'NORTH BETHLEHEM', 42.68, -73.84, 42.68, -73.84, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Wires were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771662, 201807, 27, 1255, 201807, 27, 1255, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 12:55:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 12:55:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Trained Spotter', 60, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'WNW', 'BRUNSWICK CENTER', 2, 'WNW', 'BRUNSWICK CENTER', 42.76, -73.65, 42.76, -73.65, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Numerous large trees and limbs were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771663, 201807, 27, 1300, 201807, 27, 1300, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 13:00:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Trained Spotter', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'NW', 'BRUNSWICK CENTER', 2, 'NW', 'BRUNSWICK CENTER', 42.77, -73.65, 42.77, -73.65, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Powerlines, a power pole, and large tree limbs were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (733801, 201803, 3, 100, 201803, 3, 1015, 122421, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'March', 'Flood', 'PHI', '03-MAR-18 01:00:00', 'EST-5', '03-MAR-18 10:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'WNW', 'MILLSTONE', 1, 'ENE', 'GRIGGSTOWN', 40.5052, -74.5922, 40.4526, -74.6068, 'A cold front stalled across the region on March 1st. Meanwhile, a wave of low pressure developed along this front in the Ohio Valley and move east,  deepening just  southeast of Long Island on March 2nd. This large and very deep area of low pressure moved slowly east over the open waters of the North Atlantic Ocean through Sunday March 4th. This lead to a variety of weather hazards during this time frame.||Strong Northwest winds with gusts up to around 60 mph occurred on March 2nd and 3rd. This led to widespread damage to trees and power lines, causing extensive power outages across the region.||Minor coastal flooding over multiple tide cycles occurred along the New Jersey coast March 2nd through 4th. Moderate flooding occurred during the morning high tide of Saturday the 3rd in Monmouth County, most of the NJ oceanfront Saturday evening and again Sunday morning the 4th. Conversely, blowout tides occurred in portions of Delaware Bay late on March 2nd into the 3rd.||Heavy rainfall occurred in New Jersey and Eastern Pennsylvania on March 1st and 2nd, with widespread rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches. This resulted in flooding along the North Branch of the Rancocas Creek in Burlington County, the Millstone River at Blackwells Mills in Somerset County, and the Neshanic River in Southeastern Hunterdon County. In addition, areal and minor small stream flooding also occurred.||As the rain changed to snow on the 2nd, localized heavy snowfall occurred, particularly over the higher elevations. Southeast of the New Jersey Turnpike and Interstate 95, up to around 3 inches of snowfall was observed. To the Northwest of the New Jersey Turnpike and Interstate 95, up to around 6 inches of snow was measured with localized amounts of around 9 inches. Higher elevations mainly to the north of Interstate 80 in New Jersey generally reported greater than 9 inches of snow, with amounts ranging from 10 to 18 inches generally around 1,000 feet and above.', 'The Millstone River at Blackwells Mills affecting Somerset County reached flood stage of 9.0 Feet during the morning of March 3rd. The flooding was minor in nature affecting South River Street in Millstone and River Road in Blackwells Mills.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (795254, 201812, 21, 1554, 201812, 21, 1554, 132914, 'MARYLAND', 24, 2018, 'December', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'LWX', '21-DEC-18 15:54:00', 'EST-5', '21-DEC-18 15:54:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Emergency Manager', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NW', 'GAITHERSBURG', 1, 'NW', 'GAITHERSBURG', 39.14, -77.21, 39.14, -77.21, 'A surface low tracked northeastward through the Appalachians as a potent jetstreak in the upper levels shifted northward. Unseasonably warm and moist air was transported northward and this, in combination with colder air moving in at the mid-levels, caused the|atmosphere to destabilize, resulting in showers and thunderstorms. A few of these storms became locally severe.', 'A tree was blown down blocking the right lane and shoulder of southbound I-270 near Exit 10 for westbound MD-117.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (778493, 201809, 5, 1741, 201809, 5, 1745, 129954, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '05-SEP-18 17:41:00', 'EST-5', '05-SEP-18 17:45:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '20.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'ROCKY RIVER', 0, 'N', 'ROCKY RIVER', 41.47, -81.85, 41.47, -81.85, 'Isolated thunderstorms developed during the evening of September 5th.  Downburst wind gusts of at least 60 mph caused damage in Medina and Cuyahoga Counties.', 'Thunderstorm wind gusts downed a few trees in Rocky River.  Power lines were also downed resulting in some power outages.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (778490, 201809, 4, 1414, 201809, 4, 1414, 129953, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '04-SEP-18 14:14:00', 'EST-5', '04-SEP-18 14:14:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'ESE', 'MECHANICSVILLE', 1, 'ESE', 'MECHANICSVILLE', 41.7415, -80.8745, 41.7415, -80.8745, 'An isolated thunderstorm developed over Ashtabula County and caused some minor damage.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed a tree near the intersection of Tote Road and Asegra Drive.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (778491, 201809, 3, 1420, 201809, 3, 1420, 129953, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '03-SEP-18 14:20:00', 'EST-5', '03-SEP-18 14:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SSW', 'AUSTINBURG', 1, 'SSW', 'AUSTINBURG', 41.7527, -80.8567, 41.7527, -80.8567, 'An isolated thunderstorm developed over Ashtabula County and caused some minor damage.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed a tree on Lampson Road just west of State Route 45.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (778492, 201809, 5, 1810, 201809, 5, 1815, 129954, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '05-SEP-18 18:10:00', 'EST-5', '05-SEP-18 18:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '15.00K', '0.00K', 'Emergency Manager', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SW', 'VALLEY CITY', 0, 'N', 'VALLEY CITY', 41.2231, -81.9624, 41.23, -81.95, 'Isolated thunderstorms developed during the evening of September 5th.  Downburst wind gusts of at least 60 mph caused damage in Medina and Cuyahoga Counties.', 'Thunderstorm downburst wind gusts of at least 60 mph downed at least trees in the Liverpool Township and Valley City areas.  Trees were reported downed at residences on Columbia, Neff and Law Roads.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (753736, 201804, 16, 700, 201804, 17, 1100, 125673, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'April', 'Flood', 'LWX', '16-APR-18 07:00:00', 'EST-5', '17-APR-18 11:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '10.00K', '0.00K', 'Emergency Manager', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 2, 'WNW', 'MOOREFIELD MUNI ARPT', 1, 'W', 'MOOREFIELD MUNI ARPT', 39.0776, -78.979, 39.0701, -78.971, 'Low pressure and its associated cold front passed through during the early morning hours of April 16th. Heavy rain of 2 to 4 inches fell in portions of the state, causing flooding mainly in Grant, Pendleton, and Hardy Counties. This water then moved downstream, causing flooding of larger rivers on the 17th and 18th.', 'The South Branch Potomac River exceeded its banks in the Moorefield area. Seven people who were camping did not move away from the river in time and had to be rescued out of 4-5 feet of water during the afternoon of the 16th. Damage occurred to the campers and cars that were in the area as the water rose. Additionally, portions of Cunningham Road and Trough Road were closed due to the flooding of the river.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (794795, 201811, 24, 1410, 201811, 24, 1416, 132837, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'November', 'Tornado', 'MHX', '24-NOV-18 14:10:00', 'EST-5', '24-NOV-18 14:16:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'NWS Storm Survey', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 'S', 'BROAD CREEK', 0, 'W', 'BROAD CREEK', 34.6809, -76.9226, 34.7208, -76.926, 'A supercell thunderstorm came ashore in Carteret County and produced several tornadoes, as well as severe thunderstorm wind gusts.', 'The tornado began near the intersection of 8th street and Ocean Drive in|Emerald Isle with two houses sustaining uplift of the roof deck and|significant loss of roof covering material. Some utility lines were also|damaged along Ocean Drive. The path crossed Ocean drive through a row of|houses between 8th and 7th street. Multiple homes had siding damage |with one large work trailer turned over. It was here the worst damage |occured with one house losing large sections of the roof but the walls |were still standing. Part of the roofing material was found across |Highway 58, where damage to a boat dock occurred along Bogue Sound. As |the tornado became a waterspout over Bogue Sound it likely weakened |significantly as it crossed back over land as a tornado near Adams Lane|and Broad Creek Loop Road. Here some very minor siding damage occurred |along with some trampolines blown into a tree. Here the winds were |likely closer to an EF-0 or closer to around 80 MPH. ||Eyewitness accounts of the tornado in Emerald Isle mentioned more of a|rolling feature coming on land versus a circulation. Due to the radar|signature, narrow path and significant, intense damage just east of 8th|street the evidence pointed toward tornadic versus straight line damage.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776549, 201807, 16, 1554, 201807, 16, 1554, 129626, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Hail', 'BUF', '16-JUL-18 15:54:00', 'EST-5', '16-JUL-18 15:54:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Trained Spotter', 0.75, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'PENFIELD', 0, 'N', 'PENFIELD', 43.13, -77.48, 43.13, -77.48, 'A very warm and humid air mass was in place across western and north central New York. As is usually the case with an approaching cold front, thunderstorms fired up along a pre-frontal boundary that extended from the Lake Erie shoreline northeast to Rochester. As the storms grew northeast along this boundary, they eventually encountered an outflow boundary pushing south from Lake Ontario. The intersecting boundaries fueled more impressive storms. Given high precipitable water values, the strong updrafts in these boundary enhanced storms generated copious amounts of lightning. Low topped convection does not allow for such electrification as a deep mixed phase layer is not present. The tight clustering of these lightning cores, when combined with strong divergence at cloud top was enough to generate storms that produced wind damage.', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776567, 201807, 2, 1352, 201807, 2, 1352, 129604, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '02-JUL-18 13:52:00', 'EST-5', '02-JUL-18 13:52:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'SW', 'SANDY POND', 2, 'SW', 'SANDY POND', 43.61, -76.2, 43.61, -76.2, 'The region was in an unusually warm and moist air mass with a mid-level ridge across the mid-Atlantic and an upper level trough well to the north across Hudson Bay. Surface dew points were near 70 with impressive CAPE values near 2000 J/Kg. The trigger was a subtle pre-frontal trough from upstream convection and lake breeze boundaries. Storms started to develop early in the afternoon along the lake breeze east of Lake Erie. These quickly expanded to south and east of Lake Ontario and began to accelerate eastward later in the afternoon. Numerous storms displayed impressive cores aloft on radar with damaging winds following the descent of these cores. In addition to severe weather, the 12Z Buffalo sounding had a precipitable water value of 1.75 inches, which probably reached 2 inches in some spots. Some flash flooding was the result.', 'A tree and wires down on a camp on Rainbow Showers Road near Lake Ontario in the Town of Richland.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776568, 201807, 2, 1417, 201807, 2, 1417, 129604, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '02-JUL-18 14:17:00', 'EST-5', '02-JUL-18 14:17:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NW', 'CONSTANTIA SHRWD ARP', 1, 'NW', 'CONSTANTIA SHRWD ARP', 43.33, -76.03, 43.33, -76.03, 'The region was in an unusually warm and moist air mass with a mid-level ridge across the mid-Atlantic and an upper level trough well to the north across Hudson Bay. Surface dew points were near 70 with impressive CAPE values near 2000 J/Kg. The trigger was a subtle pre-frontal trough from upstream convection and lake breeze boundaries. Storms started to develop early in the afternoon along the lake breeze east of Lake Erie. These quickly expanded to south and east of Lake Ontario and began to accelerate eastward later in the afternoon. Numerous storms displayed impressive cores aloft on radar with damaging winds following the descent of these cores. In addition to severe weather, the 12Z Buffalo sounding had a precipitable water value of 1.75 inches, which probably reached 2 inches in some spots. Some flash flooding was the result.', 'A tree down on wires near the intersection of County Route 23B and 26 in the Town of West Monroe.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755003, 201807, 3, 1740, 201807, 3, 1740, 125935, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 17:40:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 17:40:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Department of Highways', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'ESE', 'RANCOCAS WOODS', 2, 'ESE', 'RANCOCAS WOODS', 40.01, -74.85, 40.01, -74.85, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southwestern New Jersey on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell along the Interstate 95/New Jersey Turnpike Corridor in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'Tree reported down on interstate 295 near the Rancocas Road exit. Time estimated by radar.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755391, 201807, 3, 1500, 201807, 3, 1630, 125935, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 15:00:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 16:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'W', 'LINCOLN PARK', 0, 'E', 'LINCOLN PARK', 40.9319, -74.3141, 40.9307, -74.2921, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southwestern New Jersey on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell along the Interstate 95/New Jersey Turnpike Corridor in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'Widespread roadway flooding in Lincoln Park.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755394, 201807, 3, 1730, 201807, 3, 1900, 125935, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 17:30:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 19:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'VERGA', 1, 'E', 'VERGA', 39.8738, -75.1288, 39.8709, -75.125, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southwestern New Jersey on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell along the Interstate 95/New Jersey Turnpike Corridor in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'Several streets in Westville were reported under water.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755396, 201807, 3, 1720, 201807, 3, 1850, 125935, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 17:20:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 18:50:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'NW', 'PRINCETON JCT', 0, 'SE', 'PRINCETON JCT', 40.3224, -74.6231, 40.318, -74.6171, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southwestern New Jersey on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell along the Interstate 95/New Jersey Turnpike Corridor in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'There was flooding at and around the Princeton Junction train station in West Windsor Township.  Sections of the parking lot were under water and a pedestrian tunnel was flooded.  Also, there was flooding on Wallace Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758381, 201807, 1, 2030, 201807, 1, 2115, 126495, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'RLX', '01-JUL-18 20:30:00', 'EST-5', '01-JUL-18 21:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'N', 'PROCTORVILLE', 1, 'NNW', 'PROCTORVILLE', 38.44, -82.38, 38.4415, -82.3885, 'Showers and storms developed during the afternoons of the 1st and 2nd in a hot and humid airmass ahead of an approaching cold front. These storms were also aided by an approaching upper level trough. Some storms produced wind damage. The slow movement of the storms also led to some flash flooding.', 'High water closed a section of State Street in Proctorville.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758388, 201807, 2, 1700, 201807, 2, 1800, 126495, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'RLX', '02-JUL-18 17:00:00', 'EST-5', '02-JUL-18 18:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'SSW', 'GLENFORD', 1, 'SSE', 'GLENFORD', 39.8638, -82.3318, 39.8651, -82.315, 'Showers and storms developed during the afternoons of the 1st and 2nd in a hot and humid airmass ahead of an approaching cold front. These storms were also aided by an approaching upper level trough. Some storms produced wind damage. The slow movement of the storms also led to some flash flooding.', 'Minor flooding closed portions of Main Street in Glenford, and also High Point Road south of Glenford.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758390, 201807, 2, 1735, 201807, 2, 2000, 126495, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'RLX', '02-JUL-18 17:35:00', 'EST-5', '02-JUL-18 20:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Trained Spotter', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 3, 'S', 'JACKSON', 2, 'ENE', 'ROADS', 39.0011, -82.627, 39.0959, -82.4946, 'Showers and storms developed during the afternoons of the 1st and 2nd in a hot and humid airmass ahead of an approaching cold front. These storms were also aided by an approaching upper level trough. Some storms produced wind damage. The slow movement of the storms also led to some flash flooding.', 'Following a couple inches of rainfall in around an hour, high water covered some roads in Jackson County. This included Main Street in Jackson and several roads in Wellston.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760475, 201807, 2, 1815, 201807, 2, 1815, 126495, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '02-JUL-18 18:15:00', 'EST-5', '02-JUL-18 18:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '5.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 45, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'CROWN CITY', 1, 'S', 'CROWN CITY', 38.59, -82.28, 38.59, -82.28, 'Showers and storms developed during the afternoons of the 1st and 2nd in a hot and humid airmass ahead of an approaching cold front. These storms were also aided by an approaching upper level trough. Some storms produced wind damage. The slow movement of the storms also led to some flash flooding.', 'A tree was blown down and fell onto a house along Mill Street.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760477, 201807, 2, 1840, 201807, 2, 1840, 126495, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '02-JUL-18 18:40:00', 'EST-5', '02-JUL-18 18:40:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'WNW', 'WILGUS', 1, 'WNW', 'WILGUS', 38.633, -82.4638, 38.633, -82.4638, 'Showers and storms developed during the afternoons of the 1st and 2nd in a hot and humid airmass ahead of an approaching cold front. These storms were also aided by an approaching upper level trough. Some storms produced wind damage. The slow movement of the storms also led to some flash flooding.', 'A few trees were blown down near the intersection of Route 141 and 775.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (759998, 201807, 22, 2010, 201807, 22, 2210, 126773, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '22-JUL-18 20:10:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 22:10:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Fire Department/Rescue', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'NE', 'COATESVILLE', 1, 'NE', 'COATESVILLE', 39.9891, -75.805, 39.9899, -75.8052, 'Showers with heavy downpours occurred in southeastern Pennsylvania during the afternoon and evening hours of July 22, 2018.  Rainfall totals of 2 to 4 inches were reported.', 'Two vehicles were trapped in flood waters in Caln Township.  A water rescue took place at Foundry Street and North 11th Avenue, and another water rescue occurred on the Lincoln Highway at North Caln Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (761134, 201807, 30, 1809, 201807, 30, 1819, 126997, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'JKL', '30-JUL-18 18:09:00', 'EST-5', '30-JUL-18 18:19:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '7.00K', NULL, 'NWS Employee', 53, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'VIRDEN', 1, 'SSE', 'STANTON', 37.8687, -83.9526, 37.83, -83.86, 'A strong thunderstorm increased in intensity and became severe as it moved out of central Kentucky into the Mountain Parkway corridor of eastern Kentucky. A narrow swath of wind damage occurred between Clay City and Stanton in Powell County, prior to the storm quickly diminishing in strength east of Stanton this evening.', 'Numerous reports of wind damage were received from a National Weather Service employee, trained storm spotter, local fire rescue, and dispatch in between Clay City and Stanton. This consisted of a plethora of trees blown down, resulting in several power outages. The roofs of a barn and mobile home were also damaged as this storm moved east along Mountain Parkway.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (762093, 201807, 30, 1530, 201807, 30, 1530, 127158, 'FLORIDA', 12, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '30-JUL-18 15:30:00', 'EST-5', '30-JUL-18 15:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 40, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'N', 'RICHLOAM', 1, 'N', 'RICHLOAM', 28.51, -82.12, 28.51, -82.12, 'Afternoon sea breeze thunderstorms developing along the Interstate 75 corridor, producing gusty winds in Hernando County.', 'Local law enforcement reported a few trees down across potions of State Road 50 causing the road to be briefly closed.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (782058, 201809, 19, 1737, 201809, 19, 1738, 130669, 'FLORIDA', 12, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'JAX', '19-SEP-18 17:37:00', 'EST-5', '19-SEP-18 17:38:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 2, 'SSE', 'JACKSONVILLE', 2, 'SSE', 'JACKSONVILLE', 30.33, -81.66, 30.3271, -81.6637, 'The combined forcing of a backdoor cold front sliding from NE to SW across the area and the more dominant east coast sea breeze over a moist and unstable airmass triggered strong storms as localized heavy rainfall.', 'At 6:37 pm, local media reported street flooding in Springfield near West 3rd Street and Main Street. At 6:38 pm, media reported that the Hart Bridge ramp from East Duval Street was closed due to flooded roadways.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (782059, 201809, 19, 1630, 201809, 19, 1630, 130669, 'FLORIDA', 12, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'JAX', '19-SEP-18 16:30:00', 'EST-5', '19-SEP-18 16:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'CHASEVILLE', 1, 'SE', 'CHASEVILLE', 30.37, -81.61, 30.37, -81.61, 'The combined forcing of a backdoor cold front sliding from NE to SW across the area and the more dominant east coast sea breeze over a moist and unstable airmass triggered strong storms as localized heavy rainfall.', 'Tree debris was blown down along University Blvd near Blue Cypress Park.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760665, 201807, 18, 1329, 201807, 18, 1329, 126911, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '18-JUL-18 13:29:00', 'EST-5', '18-JUL-18 13:29:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'AWOS', 40, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 4, 'N', 'SATELLITE BEACH', 4, 'N', 'SATELLITE BEACH', 28.23, -80.598, 28.23, -80.598, 'A mid-level trough was located near the eastern seaboard with a weak extension into the southeastern states. This kept the Atlantic high pressure ridge suppressed across south Florida and provided low-to-mid level southwest wind flow. Moisture was abundant across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Scattered to numerous showers developed along the west coast sea breeze and pushed across the state through the afternoon. With the stout southwest flow, the east coast sea breeze was pinned along the east coast for most of the day. When the two sea breezes collided near the east coast, the strongest storms developed and pushed east across Brevard County. Several of these storms produced strong wind gusts along the intracoastal waters.', 'The AWOS at Patrick Air Force Base (KCOF) measured a peak wind gust of 40 knots from the west-southwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760667, 201807, 18, 1339, 201807, 18, 1339, 126911, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '18-JUL-18 13:39:00', 'EST-5', '18-JUL-18 13:39:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 37, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 3, 'WSW', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 3, 'WSW', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 28.36, -80.65, 28.36, -80.65, 'A mid-level trough was located near the eastern seaboard with a weak extension into the southeastern states. This kept the Atlantic high pressure ridge suppressed across south Florida and provided low-to-mid level southwest wind flow. Moisture was abundant across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Scattered to numerous showers developed along the west coast sea breeze and pushed across the state through the afternoon. With the stout southwest flow, the east coast sea breeze was pinned along the east coast for most of the day. When the two sea breezes collided near the east coast, the strongest storms developed and pushed east across Brevard County. Several of these storms produced strong wind gusts along the intracoastal waters.', 'Weatherflow site XCCB on the Banana River near State Road 520 on Merritt Island measured a peak wind gust of 37 knots from the west.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760669, 201807, 18, 1440, 201807, 18, 1440, 126911, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '18-JUL-18 14:40:00', 'EST-5', '18-JUL-18 14:40:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Buoy', 47, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'BUOY 41009', 0, 'N', 'BUOY 41009', 28.52, -80.17, 28.52, -80.17, 'A mid-level trough was located near the eastern seaboard with a weak extension into the southeastern states. This kept the Atlantic high pressure ridge suppressed across south Florida and provided low-to-mid level southwest wind flow. Moisture was abundant across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Scattered to numerous showers developed along the west coast sea breeze and pushed across the state through the afternoon. With the stout southwest flow, the east coast sea breeze was pinned along the east coast for most of the day. When the two sea breezes collided near the east coast, the strongest storms developed and pushed east across Brevard County. Several of these storms produced strong wind gusts along the intracoastal waters.', 'Buoy 41009 measured a peak wind gust of 47 knots from the west-southwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763459, 201807, 22, 1523, 201807, 22, 1523, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 15:23:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 15:23:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'AWOS', 41, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 7, 'N', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 7, 'N', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 28.477, -80.594, 28.477, -80.594, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'The AWOS at the Cape Canaveral Air Force Station Skid Strip (KXMR) measured a peak wind gust of 41 knots from the northwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763460, 201807, 22, 1525, 201807, 22, 1525, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 15:25:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 15:25:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 41, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'SSE', 'MELBOURNE BEACH', 2, 'SSE', 'MELBOURNE BEACH', 28.05, -80.56, 28.05, -80.56, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'A mesonet site near Melbourne Beach on the Indian River measured a peak wind gust of 41 knots from the north.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771664, 201807, 27, 1230, 201807, 27, 1230, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 12:30:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 12:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Social Media', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SW', 'NEWTONVILLE', 1, 'SW', 'NEWTONVILLE', 42.71, -73.77, 42.71, -73.77, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Large tree limbs were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771665, 201807, 27, 1325, 201807, 27, 1325, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 13:25:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:25:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'NWS Employee', 60, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'NW', 'ALBANY', 2, 'NW', 'ALBANY', 42.6706, -73.7981, 42.6706, -73.7981, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Several large trees uprooted in the Melrose neighborhood. One tree fell on a house and resulted in significant roof damage.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771666, 201807, 27, 1325, 201807, 27, 1325, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 13:25:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:25:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Trained Spotter', 60, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'NW', 'ALBANY', 2, 'NW', 'ALBANY', 42.6671, -73.8046, 42.6671, -73.8046, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Several large limbs were down and trees were uprooted in the Buckingham Pond neighborhood.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (790224, 201810, 2, 2220, 201810, 2, 2220, 129857, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'October', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'OKX', '02-OCT-18 22:20:00', 'EST-5', '02-OCT-18 22:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Social Media', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'ENE', 'CENTRAL ISLIP', 2, 'ENE', 'CENTRAL ISLIP', 40.7894, -73.1507, 40.7894, -73.1507, 'An approaching cold front triggered severe thunderstorms across southeastern New York, they produced 3 tornadoes across Rockland, Westchester and Suffolk Counties.', 'Tree reported down on Veterans Highway between Connectquot Avenue and 5th Avenue.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771757, 201807, 27, 1328, 201807, 27, 1328, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 13:28:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:28:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Newspaper', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'NE', 'MENANDS', 0, 'NE', 'MENANDS', 42.705, -73.724, 42.705, -73.724, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'A large beech tree was downed in Albany Rural Cemetery, shattering several grave markers.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (730585, 201802, 10, 1828, 201802, 10, 1928, 122032, 'DELAWARE', 10, 2018, 'February', 'Flood', 'PHI', '10-FEB-18 18:28:00', 'EST-5', '10-FEB-18 19:28:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Department of Highways', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'SE', 'LITTLE HEAVEN', 1, 'SE', 'LITTLE HEAVEN', 39.04, -75.46, 39.0413, -75.4548, 'Periods of heavy rainfall developed along a slow moving frontal boundary. Rainfall across ranged from 2 to 4 inches with the highest amounts in the central parts of the state. Hazlettsville at 4.12 inches, Sandtown 3.62 inches, Magnolia 3.5 inches, Blackbird 3.75 inches, Greenwood 2.05 inches, Townsend 2.89 inches and Lincoln 2.03 inches.', 'Water was reported on route 1 south in Little Haven with lane restrictions.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (730586, 201802, 11, 1240, 201802, 11, 1340, 122032, 'DELAWARE', 10, 2018, 'February', 'Flood', 'PHI', '11-FEB-18 12:40:00', 'EST-5', '11-FEB-18 13:40:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Social Media', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'NNW', 'FIELDSBORO', 0, 'NNW', 'ODESSA', 39.4341, -75.6742, 39.4555, -75.6722, 'Periods of heavy rainfall developed along a slow moving frontal boundary. Rainfall across ranged from 2 to 4 inches with the highest amounts in the central parts of the state. Hazlettsville at 4.12 inches, Sandtown 3.62 inches, Magnolia 3.5 inches, Blackbird 3.75 inches, Greenwood 2.05 inches, Townsend 2.89 inches and Lincoln 2.03 inches.', 'Flooding at the route 13 to route 1 entrance of Roth bridge.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (730603, 201802, 11, 1014, 201802, 11, 1214, 122037, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'February', 'Flood', 'PHI', '11-FEB-18 10:14:00', 'EST-5', '11-FEB-18 12:14:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Department of Highways', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 2, 'NNE', 'CHERRY HILL', 1, 'SE', 'MERCHANTVILLE', 39.9429, -75.008, 39.9396, -75.033, 'Several waves of heavy rainfall moved along a slow moving frontal boundary which led to flooding in a few spots. Rainfall of one to four inches occurred across the state. The highest totals over three inches were in southwestern New Jersey. These include 3.99 inches at Upper Deerfield, 3.75 inches at Sewell, 3.78 inches in Sicklerville and 3.15 inches in Estell manor. On the Great Egg Harbor river at gauge at Folsom went over flood stage reaching 6.1 feet. Also The gauge at Norma on the Maurice River went over flood stage reaching 4.1 feet.', 'Flooding on highway 38 in both directions was reported.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (741927, 201804, 16, 820, 201804, 16, 955, 123554, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'April', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '16-APR-18 08:20:00', 'EST-5', '16-APR-18 09:55:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 2, 'ESE', 'MANAYUNK', 1, 'W', 'ROXBOROUGH', 40.0113, -75.2004, 40.0478, -75.2539, 'A strong backdoor cold front moved from northeast to southwest across the area late Saturday afternoon April 15th into Sunday morning April 16th. Not only was there a significant drop in temperature coinciding with the passage of the front, but also a stark difference between high temperatures on Saturday and Sunday. On Saturday, high temperatures ranged from the mid-70s to mid-80s, but only made it to the mid-30s to mid-40s on Sunday. In general, there was a 40 degree temperature drop from Saturday to Sunday! ||The backdoor front became stationary south of the region then moved northward as a warm front Sunday night into Monday morning. Meanwhile, a strong cold front approached from the west and swept across the area Monday afternoon and evening, along with an attendant area of low pressure. This robust storm system tapped large amounts of moisture, which was lifted along the warm front as overrunning precipitation, and along the cold front as a line of showers and thunderstorms. ||As a result, heavy rainfall occurred across the region. A widespread 1 to 3 inches of rainfall occurred, with localized amounts over 4 inches. This lead to flooding across portions of the area. Meanwhile, it was cold enough in the higher elevations of the Southern Poconos of Northeast Pennsylvania for freezing rain on Sunday. In particular, the Pocono Mountains Airport ASOS recorded 0.19 inches of ice accretion, and there was tree damage and power outages reported in Tobyhanna Pennsylvania.||Along the coast, an extended period of onshore flow occurred, beginning with east-northeast winds Saturday Night, which then shifted to the southeast on Sunday Night into Monday Morning April 16th. By Monday morning and afternoon, tidal flooding made its way up the Delaware River to Philadelphia as a result of the onshore flow.', 'A number of small streams and creeks left their banks, including the Wissahickon Creek.  The gauge on the Wissahickon Creek peaked at 6.07 feet, exceeding its flood stage of 5 feet.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786871, 201809, 25, 2225, 201809, 26, 230, 131527, 'RHODE ISLAND', 44, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'BOX', '25-SEP-18 22:25:00', 'EST-5', '26-SEP-18 02:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Amateur Radio', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'NNE', 'OAK LAWN', 1, 'WSW', 'CRANSTON', 41.7665, -71.473, 41.7667, -71.4712, 'A warm front approached from the south on Sept 25 and stalled just north of Massachusetts on Sept 26. This brought periods of heavy rain to Rhode Island with 3 to 5 inches observed in Providence County and Kent County. Amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell on Southern Rhode Island.', 'At 10:25 PM EST, cars were reported partly submerged in an apartment complex on Oaklawn Avenue in Cranston; flooding also took place on the property in front of the complex.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786856, 201809, 26, 110, 201809, 26, 500, 131527, 'RHODE ISLAND', 44, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'BOX', '26-SEP-18 01:10:00', 'EST-5', '26-SEP-18 05:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Amateur Radio', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'S', 'OLNEYVILLE', 1, 'S', 'OLNEYVILLE', 41.806, -71.4289, 41.8085, -71.428, 'A warm front approached from the south on Sept 25 and stalled just north of Massachusetts on Sept 26. This brought periods of heavy rain to Rhode Island with 3 to 5 inches observed in Providence County and Kent County. Amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell on Southern Rhode Island.', 'At 1:10 AM EST, Dexter Street in Providence was flooded and impassable from Althea Street to Ford Street.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786860, 201809, 26, 2346, 201809, 26, 2346, 131527, 'RHODE ISLAND', 44, 2018, 'September', 'Lightning', 'BOX', '26-SEP-18 23:46:00', 'EST-5', '26-SEP-18 23:46:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', 'Amateur Radio', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'N', 'APPONAUG', 1, 'N', 'APPONAUG', 41.7096, -71.4285, 41.7096, -71.4285, 'A warm front approached from the south on Sept 25 and stalled just north of Massachusetts on Sept 26. This brought periods of heavy rain to Rhode Island with 3 to 5 inches observed in Providence County and Kent County. Amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell on Southern Rhode Island.', 'At 11:46 PM EST, lightning struck a house at Sudbury Street in Warwick.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (753707, 201804, 16, 538, 201804, 16, 1232, 125669, 'DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA', 11, 2018, 'April', 'Flood', 'LWX', '16-APR-18 05:38:00', 'EST-5', '16-APR-18 12:32:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'WNW', 'WALTER REED', 1, 'ENE', 'TENLEYTOWN', 38.9855, -77.0537, 38.9603, -77.0466, 'Low pressure and its associated cold front passed through during the early morning hours of April 16th. Heavy rain of 1.5 to 2 inches fell in the District, causing flash flooding followed by flooding of Rock Creek which continued into early afternoon.', 'The USGS stream gauge at Rock Creek remained above 7 feet for several hours, although it was no longer rapidly rising. The peak level of 7.92 feet occurred at 1045 AM EDT.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (753739, 201804, 16, 2001, 201804, 17, 1122, 125673, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'April', 'Flood', 'LWX', '16-APR-18 20:01:00', 'EST-5', '17-APR-18 11:22:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'NNE', 'MILLESONS MILL', 2, 'E', 'MILLESON', 39.4382, -78.6778, 39.4712, -78.6447, 'Low pressure and its associated cold front passed through during the early morning hours of April 16th. Heavy rain of 2 to 4 inches fell in portions of the state, causing flooding mainly in Grant, Pendleton, and Hardy Counties. This water then moved downstream, causing flooding of larger rivers on the 17th and 18th.', 'The stream gage on the South Branch Potomac River near Springfield exceeded the 15 foot flood stage. Photo and videos show several road closures and flooding of a campground area near Springfield. The peak level of 19.44 feet was observed at 515 AM EDT on April 17th, and was the highest river level observed since 2007.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (753744, 201804, 16, 1425, 201804, 16, 2109, 125673, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'April', 'Flood', 'LWX', '16-APR-18 14:25:00', 'EST-5', '16-APR-18 21:09:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 2, 'SSE', '(MRB)SHEPHERD FLD MR', 3, 'SSE', '(MRB)SHEPHERD FLD MR', 39.3687, -77.9595, 39.3619, -77.955, 'Low pressure and its associated cold front passed through during the early morning hours of April 16th. Heavy rain of 2 to 4 inches fell in portions of the state, causing flooding mainly in Grant, Pendleton, and Hardy Counties. This water then moved downstream, causing flooding of larger rivers on the 17th and 18th.', 'The stream gage on Opequon Creek near Martinsburg exceeded the 10 foot flood stage. The observed peak level was 10.50 feet at 715 PM EDT on April 16th. At this level, Douglas Grove Road and Bowers Road are flooded, and water is covering parts of the stream access point near Golf Course Road east of Martinsburg.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769752, 201808, 7, 1547, 201808, 7, 1547, 127764, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '07-AUG-18 15:47:00', 'EST-5', '07-AUG-18 15:47:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '6.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'NEW BLOOMFIELD', 1, 'W', 'NEW BLOOMFIELD', 40.4187, -77.1929, 40.4187, -77.1929, 'A broken line of storms developed across central Pennsylvania during the afternoon hours of August 7, 2018 in a high CAPE environment as a weak shortwave crossed New England. Several reports of wind damage were received, primarily across the middle and lower Susquehanna Valley.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down multiple trees and wires in New Bloomfield.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769753, 201808, 7, 1741, 201808, 7, 1741, 127764, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '07-AUG-18 17:41:00', 'EST-5', '07-AUG-18 17:41:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '6.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SSE', 'QUARRYVILLE', 1, 'SSE', 'QUARRYVILLE', 39.8821, -76.1652, 39.8821, -76.1652, 'A broken line of storms developed across central Pennsylvania during the afternoon hours of August 7, 2018 in a high CAPE environment as a weak shortwave crossed New England. Several reports of wind damage were received, primarily across the middle and lower Susquehanna Valley.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down multiple trees and snapped trees south of Quarryville.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769754, 201808, 7, 1750, 201808, 7, 1750, 127764, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CTP', '07-AUG-18 17:50:00', 'EST-5', '07-AUG-18 17:50:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', '0.00K', 'Utility Company', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'SSW', 'CEDAR LANE', 0, 'SSW', 'CEDAR LANE', 40.0942, -76.0238, 40.0942, -76.0238, 'A broken line of storms developed across central Pennsylvania during the afternoon hours of August 7, 2018 in a high CAPE environment as a weak shortwave crossed New England. Several reports of wind damage were received, primarily across the middle and lower Susquehanna Valley.', 'A severe thunderstorm producing winds estimated near 60 mph knocked down trees onto wires on Reservoir Road south of East Earl.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (769766, 201808, 17, 1536, 201808, 17, 1536, 127767, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'August', 'Hail', 'CTP', '17-AUG-18 15:36:00', 'EST-5', '17-AUG-18 15:36:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 1.25, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'GREENCASTLE', 1, 'ENE', 'GREENCASTLE', 39.79, -77.73, 39.79, -77.73, 'Scattered storms developed across central Pennsylvania during the late afternoon and evening hours of August 17, 2018 in a moderate CAPE, moderate shear environment. A few of the storms produced wind damage across south-central Pennsylvania.', 'A severe thunderstorm produced half-dollar sized hail in Greencastle.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776165, 201807, 12, 1518, 201807, 12, 1520, 129550, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Hail', 'ILM', '12-JUL-18 15:18:00', 'EST-5', '12-JUL-18 15:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Trained Spotter', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, 'W', 'BAYMEADE', 2, 'W', 'BAYMEADE', 34.2748, -77.8514, 34.2748, -77.8514, 'A cold front produced strong thunderstorms with hail.', 'Quarter size hail was reported on Gordon Road, near Interstate 40.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (790159, 201810, 2, 2130, 201810, 3, 115, 132040, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'October', 'Flash Flood', 'OKX', '02-OCT-18 21:30:00', 'EST-5', '03-OCT-18 01:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'ESE', 'RIDGEWOOD', 0, 'ESE', 'RIDGEWOOD', 40.9972, -74.112, 40.9975, -74.1127, 'A warm front lifted north across the area through the day on October 2nd, leaving the local area in the warm sector. Multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms developed and moved through the region. With wet antecedent conditions from recent rainfall and plenty of available moisture as precipitable water values approached two inches, these showers and storms resulted in flash flooding across portions of northeast New Jersey. Rainfall totals across the region generally ranged from 1-3 inches, with a CoCoRaHS observer in Oakland reporting 2.30 inches.', 'The Hohokus Brook rose above its flood stage of 3.0ft at 10:30pm EDT October 2nd, crested at a height of 3.51 ft at 11:00pm EDT, and fell back below flood stage at 2:15am EDT October 3rd.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (790155, 201810, 2, 2048, 201810, 2, 2118, 132040, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'October', 'Flash Flood', 'OKX', '02-OCT-18 20:48:00', 'EST-5', '02-OCT-18 21:18:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'E', 'OAKLAND', 1, 'E', 'OAKLAND', 41.0295, -74.2327, 41.0299, -74.2327, 'A warm front lifted north across the area through the day on October 2nd, leaving the local area in the warm sector. Multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms developed and moved through the region. With wet antecedent conditions from recent rainfall and plenty of available moisture as precipitable water values approached two inches, these showers and storms resulted in flash flooding across portions of northeast New Jersey. Rainfall totals across the region generally ranged from 1-3 inches, with a CoCoRaHS observer in Oakland reporting 2.30 inches.', 'A car was floating on Calumet Avenue in Oakland due to flooding. In addition, street flooding was reported on both Seminole Avenue and Pine Crest Drive.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775146, 201807, 6, 1201, 201807, 6, 1224, 129335, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'GSP', '06-JUL-18 12:01:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 12:24:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Emergency Manager', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'MARION', 2, 'ESE', 'PROVIDENCE', 35.686, -82, 35.619, -82.02, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed across the North Carolina mountains and foothills during the afternoon and moved into the western Piedmont by early evening. A few of the storms produced strong to damaging winds that caused tree damage, with one tree  falling on a vehicle north of Lenoir, killing one of the occupants.', 'EM reported trees blown down at Clay St and State St, on I-40 at mile markers 82 and 83, and on Goose Creek Rd.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775149, 201807, 6, 1353, 201807, 6, 1353, 129335, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'GSP', '06-JUL-18 13:53:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 13:53:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'BOSTIC', 1, 'SE', 'BOSTIC', 35.36, -81.84, 35.36, -81.84, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed across the North Carolina mountains and foothills during the afternoon and moved into the western Piedmont by early evening. A few of the storms produced strong to damaging winds that caused tree damage, with one tree  falling on a vehicle north of Lenoir, killing one of the occupants.', 'County comms reported numerous trees blown down in the Bostic area.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775344, 201807, 6, 1505, 201807, 6, 1505, 129335, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'GSP', '06-JUL-18 15:05:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 15:05:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'SW', 'STALLINGS', 2, 'SW', 'STALLINGS', 35.054, -80.722, 35.054, -80.722, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed across the North Carolina mountains and foothills during the afternoon and moved into the western Piedmont by early evening. A few of the storms produced strong to damaging winds that caused tree damage, with one tree  falling on a vehicle north of Lenoir, killing one of the occupants.', 'County comms reported multiple trees blown down near Forest Lawn Dr and Antioch Church Rd.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (793691, 201811, 7, 1755, 201811, 7, 1815, 132630, 'GEORGIA', 13, 2018, 'November', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'FFC', '07-NOV-18 17:55:00', 'EST-5', '07-NOV-18 18:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '7.00K', NULL, 'Emergency Manager', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'ESE', 'HUBER', 3, 'S', 'MYRICKS MILL', 32.6926, -83.5311, 32.7352, -83.3696, 'Thunderstorms along a slowly moving cold front produced isolated reports of damaging thunderstorm winds across central Georgia during the late afternoon and early evening.', 'The Twiggs County Emergency Manager reported several trees blown down from Huber to near Myricks Mill.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755397, 201807, 3, 1815, 201807, 3, 1915, 125935, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 18:15:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 19:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 2, 'W', 'WILLINGBORO', 1, 'N', 'CENTERTON', 40.0307, -74.9148, 40.0091, -74.8779, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southwestern New Jersey on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell along the Interstate 95/New Jersey Turnpike Corridor in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'There was widespread roadway flooding in Willingboro.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (765475, 201807, 3, 1730, 201807, 3, 1730, 125935, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Hail', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 17:30:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 17:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'NWS Employee', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'RIVERSIDE', 1, 'S', 'RIVERSIDE', 40.01, -74.95, 40.01, -74.95, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southwestern New Jersey on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell along the Interstate 95/New Jersey Turnpike Corridor in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'Nickel to quarter size hail.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755009, 201807, 3, 1827, 201807, 3, 1827, 125939, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 18:27:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 18:27:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'BERWYN', 1, 'W', 'BERWYN', 40.05, -75.43, 40.05, -75.43, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southeastern Pennsylvania on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'Tree reported down on Old Lancaster Road. Time estimated  from radar.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755011, 201807, 3, 1803, 201807, 3, 1803, 125939, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 18:03:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 18:03:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Trained Spotter', 52, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'DOWNINGTOWN', 1, 'S', 'DOWNINGTOWN', 40.01, -75.7, 40.01, -75.7, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southeastern Pennsylvania on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'A wind gust to 60 mph was reported.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755402, 201807, 3, 1800, 201807, 3, 1900, 125939, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 18:00:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 19:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Social Media', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'N', 'BERWYN', 1, 'E', 'PAOLI', 40.0559, -75.4215, 40.0509, -75.4529, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southeastern Pennsylvania on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'There was widespread roadway flooding in Berwyn and Devon.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755401, 201807, 3, 1810, 201807, 3, 2010, 125939, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '03-JUL-18 18:10:00', 'EST-5', '03-JUL-18 20:10:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Fire Department/Rescue', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'SSW', 'BRYN MAWR', 1, 'WNW', 'FOXCROFT', 40.0161, -75.3232, 40.0023, -75.3627, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage across portions of southeastern Pennsylvania on the evening of July 3.  Rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches fell in a short amount of time.  A few locations received 3 to 4 inches of rain.', 'Widespread roadway flooding occurred in Radnor Township.  There was flooding on Interstate 476 near the Villanova exit.  The flood waters left debris on the roadway.  Also, there was a water rescue on Conestoga Road near County Line Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755020, 201807, 4, 1455, 201807, 4, 1455, 125942, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '04-JUL-18 14:55:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 14:55:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'KLECKNERSVILLE', 1, 'S', 'KLECKNERSVILLE', 40.77, -75.42, 40.77, -75.42, 'Severe thunderstorms caused wind damage in the Lehigh Valley Region of Pennsylvania.  Also, rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches occurred in a short period of time.', 'Numerous reports of trees as well as wires down across the area. Time estimated from radar.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758206, 201807, 5, 1858, 201807, 5, 1858, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '05-JUL-18 18:58:00', 'EST-5', '05-JUL-18 18:58:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'ESE', '(CRW) YEAGER ARPT', 1, 'ESE', '(CRW) YEAGER ARPT', 38.3632, -81.5849, 38.3632, -81.5849, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Several trees were blown down along Greenbrier Street.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758209, 201807, 5, 1912, 201807, 5, 1912, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '05-JUL-18 19:12:00', 'EST-5', '05-JUL-18 19:12:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', 'Utility Company', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'COAL FORK', 1, 'SE', 'COAL FORK', 38.312, -81.5077, 38.312, -81.5077, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'A tree was blown down along Big Coal Fork Road. The tree also brought down a power line.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758210, 201807, 6, 1303, 201807, 6, 1303, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '06-JUL-18 13:03:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 13:03:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'BRANCHLAND', 0, 'N', 'BRANCHLAND', 38.22, -82.2, 38.22, -82.2, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Several trees were blown down along Route 10 in Branchland.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758211, 201807, 6, 1328, 201807, 6, 1328, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '06-JUL-18 13:28:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 13:28:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'RANGER', 1, 'W', 'RANGER', 38.12, -82.19, 38.12, -82.19, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'A few trees were blown down along Route 10 in Ranger.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758394, 201807, 4, 1759, 201807, 4, 2000, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 17:59:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 20:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'COFFMAN', 1, 'ENE', 'BLUEVILLE', 39.3858, -80.0236, 39.3531, -79.9804, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Heavy rain caused flooding on several streets in Grafton, and also along Country Club Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760480, 201807, 4, 1510, 201807, 4, 1510, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 15:10:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 15:10:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'SE', 'RICHWOOD MUNI ARPT', 0, 'SE', 'RICHWOOD MUNI ARPT', 38.2665, -80.6267, 38.2665, -80.6267, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Multiple trees were blown down in the Craigsville, Nettie and Richwood area.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760484, 201807, 4, 1550, 201807, 4, 1550, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 15:50:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 15:50:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'NE', 'RAMAGE', 0, 'NE', 'RAMAGE', 37.9835, -81.8263, 37.9835, -81.8263, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Several trees were blown down on Six Mile Road. One also brought down a set of power lines.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (759358, 201807, 22, 1840, 201807, 23, 40, 126681, 'MARYLAND', 24, 2018, 'July', 'Flash Flood', 'PHI', '22-JUL-18 18:40:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 00:40:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'WSW', 'ELKTON', 1, 'ENE', 'FAIR HILL', 39.598, -75.8382, 39.7036, -75.8491, 'Showers with heavy downpours occurred in northeastern Maryland during the afternoon and evening hours of July 22, 2018. Rainfall totals of 2 to 4 inches were reported.', 'Moderate flooding occurred along the Big Elk Creek.  Several businesses on South Bridge Street in Elkton were flooded with about a foot of water.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760027, 201807, 23, 327, 201807, 23, 327, 126777, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '23-JUL-18 03:27:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 03:27:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'ASOS', 40, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 8, 'NW', 'OLD TAMPA BAY', 8, 'NW', 'OLD TAMPA BAY', 27.9126, -82.6856, 27.9126, -82.6856, 'A strong outflow boundary moved south from the Florida Panhandle through the eastern Gulf of Mexico during the overnight and early morning hours of the 23rd. Numerous thunderstorms developed along the outflow, producing marine wind gusts along the coast.', 'The ASOS at St. Pete-Clearwater International Airport (KPIE) recorded a 40 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760033, 201807, 23, 342, 201807, 23, 342, 126777, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '23-JUL-18 03:42:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 03:42:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'AWOS', 34, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 3, 'ESE', 'OLD TAMPA BAY', 3, 'ESE', 'OLD TAMPA BAY', 27.8407, -82.5315, 27.8407, -82.5315, 'A strong outflow boundary moved south from the Florida Panhandle through the eastern Gulf of Mexico during the overnight and early morning hours of the 23rd. Numerous thunderstorms developed along the outflow, producing marine wind gusts along the coast.', 'The AWOS at MacDill Air Force Base (KMCF) recorded a 34 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760038, 201807, 23, 354, 201807, 23, 354, 126777, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '23-JUL-18 03:54:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 03:54:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 38, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 1, 'S', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 27.6, -82.65, 27.6, -82.65, 'A strong outflow boundary moved south from the Florida Panhandle through the eastern Gulf of Mexico during the overnight and early morning hours of the 23rd. Numerous thunderstorms developed along the outflow, producing marine wind gusts along the coast.', 'The WeatherFlow station on the southern Sunshine Skyway Fishing Pier (XSKY) recorded a 38 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760039, 201807, 23, 356, 201807, 23, 356, 126777, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '23-JUL-18 03:56:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 03:56:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 49, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 7, 'W', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 7, 'W', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 27.61, -82.76, 27.61, -82.76, 'A strong outflow boundary moved south from the Florida Panhandle through the eastern Gulf of Mexico during the overnight and early morning hours of the 23rd. Numerous thunderstorms developed along the outflow, producing marine wind gusts along the coast.', 'The WeatherFlow station at Egmont Key (XEGM) recorded a 49 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (755222, 201807, 6, 1730, 201807, 6, 1730, 125979, 'FLORIDA', 12, 2018, 'July', 'Lightning', 'TBW', '06-JUL-18 17:30:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 17:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '45.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'ESE', 'ST JOSEPH', 1, 'ESE', 'ST JOSEPH', 28.3713, -82.2638, 28.3713, -82.2638, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed across the Florida Peninsula under deep moisture. A lightning strike from one of these storms caused a fire at an office building.', 'A fire was reported at an office building near Dade City that was suspected to have been caused by lightning. Broadcast media reported that there was nearly $50,000 in damage.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760003, 201807, 21, 1502, 201807, 21, 1502, 126775, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '21-JUL-18 15:02:00', 'EST-5', '21-JUL-18 15:02:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'C-MAN Station', 36, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 168, 'NNW', 'GASPARILLA PASS', 168, 'NNW', 'GASPARILLA PASS', 29.1359, -83.0293, 29.1359, -83.0293, 'Westerly flow to the south of a weak surface trough set up scattered showers and storms over the eastern Gulf moving onshore into the Florida Peninsula throughout the day. One of these showers produced a waterspout, and at least one other storm caused gusty winds along the coast.', 'The C-MAN station at Cedar Key (CDRF1) measured a 36 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (758189, 201807, 20, 1602, 201807, 20, 1604, 126490, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ILN', '20-JUL-18 16:02:00', 'EST-5', '20-JUL-18 16:04:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Emergency Manager', 45, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'WNW', 'PORTSMOUTH', 1, 'WNW', 'PORTSMOUTH', 38.7364, -82.995, 38.7364, -82.995, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed through the afternoon as an upper level disturbance pushed southeast into the region. A few of the storms produced damaging winds.', 'A large tree was downed onto 8th Street.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760664, 201807, 18, 1320, 201807, 18, 1320, 126911, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '18-JUL-18 13:20:00', 'EST-5', '18-JUL-18 13:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Other Federal Agency', 35, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'SSE', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 2, 'SSE', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 28.53, -80.77, 28.53, -80.77, 'A mid-level trough was located near the eastern seaboard with a weak extension into the southeastern states. This kept the Atlantic high pressure ridge suppressed across south Florida and provided low-to-mid level southwest wind flow. Moisture was abundant across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Scattered to numerous showers developed along the west coast sea breeze and pushed across the state through the afternoon. With the stout southwest flow, the east coast sea breeze was pinned along the east coast for most of the day. When the two sea breezes collided near the east coast, the strongest storms developed and pushed east across Brevard County. Several of these storms produced strong wind gusts along the intracoastal waters.', 'U.S. Air Force wind tower 1007 measured a peak wind gust of 35 knots from the west-northwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760666, 201807, 18, 1330, 201807, 18, 1330, 126911, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '18-JUL-18 13:30:00', 'EST-5', '18-JUL-18 13:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Other Federal Agency', 39, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 14, 'NNE', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 14, 'NNE', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 28.74, -80.7, 28.74, -80.7, 'A mid-level trough was located near the eastern seaboard with a weak extension into the southeastern states. This kept the Atlantic high pressure ridge suppressed across south Florida and provided low-to-mid level southwest wind flow. Moisture was abundant across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Scattered to numerous showers developed along the west coast sea breeze and pushed across the state through the afternoon. With the stout southwest flow, the east coast sea breeze was pinned along the east coast for most of the day. When the two sea breezes collided near the east coast, the strongest storms developed and pushed east across Brevard County. Several of these storms produced strong wind gusts along the intracoastal waters.', 'U.S. Air Force wind tower 0019 measured a peak wind gust of 39 knots from the west.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760679, 201807, 19, 1349, 201807, 19, 1349, 126917, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '19-JUL-18 13:49:00', 'EST-5', '19-JUL-18 13:49:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 34, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 3, 'WSW', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 3, 'WSW', 'CAPE CANAVERAL', 28.36, -80.65, 28.36, -80.65, 'Deep southwest flow was present across the Florida peninsula as a frontal trough was stalled across the Deep South and Western Atlantic, suppressing the Bermuda Ridge to the Florida Straits. Abundant moisture was present across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Diurnal heating led to scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms development across the inland peninsula, with the dominant southwest wind flow pushing the activity to the east coast. As these storms moved across the Brevard County coast they produced strong winds along the intracoastal waters near Cape Canaveral.', 'Weatherflow site XCCB on the Banana River near State Road 520 on Merritt Island measured a peak wind gust of 34 knots from the west-southwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763461, 201807, 22, 1530, 201807, 22, 1530, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 15:30:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 15:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'AWOS', 44, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 4, 'N', 'SATELLITE BEACH', 4, 'N', 'SATELLITE BEACH', 28.23, -80.598, 28.23, -80.598, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'The AWOS at Patrick Air Force Base (KCOF) measured a peak wind gust of 44 knots from the north.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763462, 201807, 22, 1537, 201807, 22, 1537, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 15:37:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 15:37:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 45, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'N', 'VALKARIA', 1, 'N', 'VALKARIA', 27.98, -80.55, 27.98, -80.55, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'A mesonet site near Grant on the Indian River measured a peak wind gust of 45 knots from the north-northwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (781023, 201809, 23, 1700, 201809, 23, 2200, 130482, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'RLX', '23-SEP-18 17:00:00', 'EST-5', '23-SEP-18 22:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'SSE', 'GARNER', 0, 'WSW', 'GARNER', 38.2972, -82.7287, 38.2982, -82.7385, 'A stalled front across southern Kentucky on the 23rd led to a prolonged period of moderate to heavy rain, creating flooding issues.', 'Flooding along Long Branch Creek closed the intersection of SR 854 and Long Branch Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (781048, 201809, 9, 1300, 201809, 9, 1500, 129567, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'RLX', '09-SEP-18 13:00:00', 'EST-5', '09-SEP-18 15:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', 'State Official', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'NNE', 'HOPEWELL', 3, 'WNW', 'SAMARIA', 38.4038, -82.8968, 38.4293, -83.0033, 'Moisture from the remnants of Tropical Storm Gordon led to a prolonged period of moderate to heavy rain. This caused some flooding in extreme northeast Kentucky.', 'High water impacted the intersection of Route 1 and Route 784.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (781055, 201809, 9, 1412, 201809, 9, 1800, 129567, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'RLX', '09-SEP-18 14:12:00', 'EST-5', '09-SEP-18 18:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 2, 'N', 'SOLDIER', 1, 'S', 'WOLF', 38.2736, -83.2945, 38.3645, -83.1204, 'Moisture from the remnants of Tropical Storm Gordon led to a prolonged period of moderate to heavy rain. This caused some flooding in extreme northeast Kentucky.', 'Minor flooding occurred on several roads in Carter County including Highway 174 near Olive Hill and Highway 1 near Grayson.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (782487, 201809, 25, 630, 201809, 26, 445, 130764, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'RLX', '25-SEP-18 06:30:00', 'EST-5', '26-SEP-18 04:45:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'NE', 'MACKSBURG', 1, 'ENE', 'MACKSBURG', 39.6345, -81.466, 39.6343, -81.4592, 'On the 23rd a surface boundary was stalled across southern West Virginia. It slowly moved north as a warm front on the 24th and 25th as a surface low crossed the region. This low then pushed a cold front through on the 26th and 27th. Atmospheric moisture was anomalously high throughout the period, leading to multiple rounds of moderate to heavy rain which caused some flooding.', 'Duck Creek in Macksburg flooded, causing some flooding on Broad Street as well as low lying areas and camps along the creek. The stream gage at Macksburg indicated the creek rose above is 13 foot flood stage just before sunrise on the 25th, crested at 13.9 feet late that afternoon, and returned to its banks in the pre-dawn hours of the 26th.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (754314, 201807, 1, 1611, 201807, 1, 1613, 125774, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ILN', '01-JUL-18 16:11:00', 'EST-5', '01-JUL-18 16:13:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', '0.00K', 'Emergency Manager', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'WHEELERSBURG', 1, 'S', 'WHEELERSBURG', 38.72, -82.83, 38.72, -82.83, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed during the afternoon hours in a hot and humid air mass that was in place across the Ohio Valley.', 'Six trees were downed onto roads in the Wheelersburg area.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776749, 201807, 28, 730, 201807, 28, 734, 129675, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Waterspout', 'ILM', '28-JUL-18 07:30:00', 'EST-5', '28-JUL-18 07:34:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 'NE', 'SHERMAN WRECK', 3, 'NE', 'SHERMAN WRECK', 33.76, -78.5, 33.76, -78.5, 'The media spotted a waterspout off of Sunset Beach.', 'The media reported and photographed a waterspout south of Sunset Beach.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771915, 201809, 2, 1444, 201809, 2, 1444, 128694, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'September', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '02-SEP-18 14:44:00', 'EST-5', '02-SEP-18 14:44:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Buoy', 34, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 4, 'NNE', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 4, 'NNE', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 27.663, -82.618, 27.663, -82.618, 'Persistent easterly flow allowed thunderstorms to develop across the Florida Peninsula during the early afternoon and shift west into the eastern Gulf of Mexico through the early evening. Some of these storms caused gusty winds along the coast. Another storm produced a waterspout that was spotted over the Tampa Bay.', 'The NOS buoy at Middle Tampa Bay (C-CUT) measured a wind gust of 34 knots.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771916, 201809, 2, 1441, 201809, 2, 1441, 128694, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'September', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '02-SEP-18 14:41:00', 'EST-5', '02-SEP-18 14:41:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 36, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 7, 'W', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 7, 'W', 'LOWER TAMPA BAY', 27.61, -82.76, 27.61, -82.76, 'Persistent easterly flow allowed thunderstorms to develop across the Florida Peninsula during the early afternoon and shift west into the eastern Gulf of Mexico through the early evening. Some of these storms caused gusty winds along the coast. Another storm produced a waterspout that was spotted over the Tampa Bay.', 'The WeatherFlow station on Egmont Key (XEGM) recorded a 42 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (772526, 201809, 3, 1225, 201809, 3, 1225, 128809, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'September', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '03-SEP-18 12:25:00', 'EST-5', '03-SEP-18 12:25:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'ASOS', 43, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 6, 'W', 'MIDDLE TAMPA BAY', 6, 'W', 'MIDDLE TAMPA BAY', 27.7685, -82.6257, 27.7685, -82.6257, 'As Tropical Storm Gordon moved west-northwest through the eastern Gulf of Mexico, deep moisture and easterly winds northeast of the storms led to scattered thunderstorms moving west across parts of the Florida Peninsula. Some of these storms produced gusty winds along the coast.', 'The ASOS at Albert Whitted Airport (KSPG) measured a 43 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775582, 201809, 6, 1619, 201809, 6, 1619, 129448, 'FLORIDA', 12, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '06-SEP-18 16:19:00', 'EST-5', '06-SEP-18 16:19:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '15.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 40, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'WNW', 'RUSKIN', 1, 'WNW', 'RUSKIN', 27.714, -82.451, 27.714, -82.451, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed under easterly flow. One of these storms produced a downburst wind gust that caused damage along the Tampa Bay in Hillsborough County.', 'A tree was knocked down and some roofing was removed from one mobile home due to downburst winds.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775587, 201809, 3, 1251, 201809, 3, 1251, 128809, 'GULF OF MEXICO', 85, 2018, 'September', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '03-SEP-18 12:51:00', 'EST-5', '03-SEP-18 12:51:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'ASOS', 39, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SSE', 'LONGBOAT KEY', 1, 'SSE', 'LONGBOAT KEY', 27.4015, -82.5586, 27.4015, -82.5586, 'As Tropical Storm Gordon moved west-northwest through the eastern Gulf of Mexico, deep moisture and easterly winds northeast of the storms led to scattered thunderstorms moving west across parts of the Florida Peninsula. Some of these storms produced gusty winds along the coast.', 'The ASOS at Sarasota-Bradenton International Airport measured a 39 knot thunderstorm wind gust.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771668, 201807, 27, 1328, 201807, 27, 1328, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 13:28:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:28:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Department of Highways', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SSW', 'LOUDONVILLE', 1, 'SSW', 'LOUDONVILLE', 42.6913, -73.7532, 42.6913, -73.7532, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'A tree was downed blocking a lane of Route 9 at Aspinwall Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771669, 201807, 27, 1325, 201807, 27, 1325, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 13:25:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:25:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'NWS Employee', 60, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NW', 'ALBANY', 1, 'NW', 'ALBANY', 42.6636, -73.792, 42.6636, -73.792, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Several large limbs were downed and trees were uprooted in the Pine Hills neighborhood.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771671, 201807, 27, 1348, 201807, 27, 1348, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 13:48:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:48:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Social Media', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'WSW', 'WYNANTSKILL', 1, 'WSW', 'WYNANTSKILL', 42.6965, -73.6427, 42.6965, -73.6427, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'A large tree was downed on Main Avenue.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786543, 201809, 21, 1650, 201809, 21, 1650, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 16:50:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 16:50:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '5.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'NE', 'BELLEVIEW', 2, 'NE', 'BELLEVIEW', 42.15, -79.31, 42.15, -79.31, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'Trees and wires were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786544, 201809, 21, 1650, 201809, 21, 1650, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 16:50:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 16:50:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '3.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'HAMLET', 1, 'W', 'HAMLET', 42.37, -79.15, 42.37, -79.15, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'Trees and wires were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786545, 201809, 21, 1654, 201809, 21, 1654, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 16:54:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 16:54:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'N', 'GERRY', 1, 'N', 'GERRY', 42.19, -79.25, 42.19, -79.25, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'A tree was reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786546, 201809, 21, 1628, 201809, 21, 1628, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 16:28:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 16:28:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'C-MAN Station', 53, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NW', 'DUNKIRK', 1, 'NW', 'DUNKIRK', 42.49, -79.35, 42.49, -79.35, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786547, 201809, 21, 1634, 201809, 21, 1634, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 16:34:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 16:34:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NW', 'GETZVILLE', 1, 'NW', 'GETZVILLE', 43.03, -78.77, 43.03, -78.77, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'A tree was reported down blocking Tonawanda Creek by the media.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786548, 201809, 21, 1640, 201809, 21, 1640, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 16:40:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 16:40:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'EBENEZER', 1, 'S', 'EBENEZER', 42.84, -78.75, 42.84, -78.75, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'Trees were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (773128, 201807, 23, 1931, 201807, 23, 1939, 128934, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '23-JUL-18 19:31:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 19:39:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '25.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'BRUNSWICK', 0, 'N', 'HINCKLEY', 41.23, -81.83, 41.23, -81.75, 'A trough of low pressure moved across Ohio on July 24rd causing a broken line of showers and thunderstorms to develop.  There were a couple reports of damage from the stronger thunderstorms.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed several trees and large limbs in the Brunswick and Hinckley areas.  Some power lines were also reported down which caused some power outages.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (773168, 201807, 26, 1835, 201807, 26, 1835, 128935, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '26-JUL-18 18:35:00', 'EST-5', '26-JUL-18 18:35:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '10.00K', '0.00K', 'Social Media', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'LORAIN', 0, 'N', 'LORAIN', 41.47, -82.18, 41.47, -82.18, 'A cold front swept east across the Upper Ohio Valley on July 26th causing a lines of thunderstorms to develop.  A lot of storm damage was reported along the central lakeshore counties of Lake Erie.  Sandusky in Erie County sustained the worst of the damage.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed a tree in the City of Lorain.  The tree landed on a parked car causing considerable damage.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (743456, 201803, 19, 1836, 201803, 19, 1846, 123500, 'GEORGIA', 13, 2018, 'March', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'FFC', '19-MAR-18 18:36:00', 'EST-5', '19-MAR-18 18:46:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '10.00K', NULL, 'Emergency Manager', 55, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 3, 'S', 'LAURENS HILL', 3, 'SSE', 'LAURENS HILL', 32.4795, -83.1238, 32.473, -83.1152, 'Widespread severe thunderstorms broke out across central and north Georgia during the evening hours of March 19th, through the early morning hours of the 20th as a warm front lifted north across the region ahead of a strong storm system developing across the lower Mississippi Valley.', 'The Laurens County Emergency Manager reported multiple trees blown down along Lord Dexter Road between Lord Road and Chicken Road. Dime size hail was also reported in this area.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (749809, 201803, 30, 1200, 201803, 30, 1239, 125023, 'ATLANTIC NORTH', 88, 2018, 'March', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'LWX', '30-MAR-18 12:00:00', 'EST-5', '30-MAR-18 12:39:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Mesonet', 34, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'HAMPSTEAD HILL ACADEMY (BLMHH)', 0, 'N', 'HAMPSTEAD HILL ACADEMY (BLMHH)', 39.29, -76.58, 39.29, -76.58, 'A strong cold front passed through. Gusty showers developed along and ahead of the boundary.', 'Wind gusts in excess of 30 knots were reported at the Hampstead Hill Academy.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (749811, 201803, 30, 1206, 201803, 30, 1206, 125023, 'ATLANTIC NORTH', 88, 2018, 'March', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'LWX', '30-MAR-18 12:06:00', 'EST-5', '30-MAR-18 12:06:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Buoy', 34, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'BALTIMORE KEY BRIDGE (FSKM2)', 0, 'N', 'BALTIMORE KEY BRIDGE (FSKM2)', 39.22, -76.53, 39.22, -76.53, 'A strong cold front passed through. Gusty showers developed along and ahead of the boundary.', 'Wind gusts in excess of 30 knots were reported at the Key Bridge.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (749812, 201803, 30, 1211, 201803, 30, 1211, 125023, 'ATLANTIC NORTH', 88, 2018, 'March', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'LWX', '30-MAR-18 12:11:00', 'EST-5', '30-MAR-18 12:11:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'ASOS', 37, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', '(KMTN)MARTIN STATE AIRPORT', 0, 'N', '(KMTN)MARTIN STATE AIRPORT', 39.33, -76.42, 39.33, -76.42, 'A strong cold front passed through. Gusty showers developed along and ahead of the boundary.', 'A wind gust of 37 knots was reported at Martin State.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (749819, 201803, 30, 1231, 201803, 30, 1231, 125023, 'ATLANTIC NORTH', 88, 2018, 'March', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'LWX', '30-MAR-18 12:31:00', 'EST-5', '30-MAR-18 12:31:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Buoy', 34, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'HAVRE DE GRACE (HAVDG)', 0, 'N', 'HAVRE DE GRACE (HAVDG)', 39.55, -76.11, 39.55, -76.11, 'A strong cold front passed through. Gusty showers developed along and ahead of the boundary.', 'A wind gust in excess of 30 knots was reported.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776166, 201807, 12, 1500, 201807, 12, 1500, 129550, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Lightning', 'ILM', '12-JUL-18 15:00:00', 'EST-5', '12-JUL-18 15:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '20.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'WILMINGTON', 1, 'ENE', 'WILMINGTON', 34.2359, -77.9163, 34.2359, -77.9163, 'A cold front produced strong thunderstorms with hail.', 'Lightning started a structural fire on Keaton Ave in downtown Wilmington.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776167, 201807, 1, 1445, 201807, 1, 1447, 129551, 'SOUTH CAROLINA', 45, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ILM', '01-JUL-18 14:45:00', 'EST-5', '01-JUL-18 14:47:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 56, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'SSE', 'RED HILL EAST', 2, 'SSE', 'RED HILL EAST', 33.795, -79.0117, 33.795, -79.0117, 'A cold front produced strong thunderstorms with hail.', 'A tree and large branches were blown down on the Coastal Carolina University campus.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776171, 201807, 20, 736, 201807, 20, 739, 129554, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Funnel Cloud', 'ILM', '20-JUL-18 07:36:00', 'EST-5', '20-JUL-18 07:39:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'CAROLINA BEACH', 1, 'ENE', 'CAROLINA BEACH', 34.0336, -77.8893, 34.0336, -77.8893, 'A funnel cloud was reported near Carolina Beach.', 'A funnel cloud was reported just offshore from Carolina Beach.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776429, 201807, 22, 2356, 201807, 23, 0, 129612, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ILM', '22-JUL-18 23:56:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'SE', 'BAYMEADE', 2, 'SE', 'BAYMEADE', 34.25, -77.8, 34.25, -77.8, 'A stationary front produced strong nocturnal storms.', 'An officer reported a large limb down on New Center Dr.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776441, 201807, 24, 239, 201807, 24, 241, 129618, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'ILM', '24-JUL-18 02:39:00', 'EST-5', '24-JUL-18 02:41:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'C-MAN Station', 44, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 9, 'WSW', 'CHERRY GROVE INLET', 9, 'WSW', 'CHERRY GROVE INLET', 33.79, -78.74, 33.79, -78.74, 'A slow moving frontal boundary produced strong storms at the coast.', 'A 51 mph gust was measured at the Briarcliffe Acres mesonet site.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776747, 201807, 26, 1320, 201807, 26, 1325, 129673, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Waterspout', 'ILM', '26-JUL-18 13:20:00', 'EST-5', '26-JUL-18 13:25:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'N', 'CAROLINA BEACH NAVIGATIONAL BUOY', 1, 'N', 'CAROLINA BEACH NAVIGATIONAL BUOY', 34.05, -77.87, 34.05, -77.87, 'A coastal trough produced a waterspout off the coast of Carolina Beach.', 'A coastal trough produced a waterspout off the coast of Carolina Beach fishing pier.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776748, 201807, 27, 629, 201807, 27, 631, 129674, 'SOUTH CAROLINA', 45, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ILM', '27-JUL-18 06:29:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 06:31:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '10.00K', '0.00K', 'Utility Company', 56, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'E', 'DUNBAR', 2, 'E', 'DUNBAR', 34.53, -79.51, 34.53, -79.51, 'An approaching cold front produced a strong storm in Marlboro County.', 'The Utility Company reported trees down on power lines near Currie Road and SC-9 west of Minturn, SC. Damage to electrical equipment led to an estimated 175 power outages.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775507, 201807, 6, 1535, 201807, 6, 1535, 129335, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'GSP', '06-JUL-18 15:35:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 15:35:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'MT HOLLY', 1, 'SSE', 'BELMONT', 35.29, -81.011, 35.239, -81.042, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed across the North Carolina mountains and foothills during the afternoon and moved into the western Piedmont by early evening. A few of the storms produced strong to damaging winds that caused tree damage, with one tree  falling on a vehicle north of Lenoir, killing one of the occupants.', 'County comms reported a tree blown down along Highland St in Mount Holly and another tree down on Central Ave in Belmont.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775509, 201807, 6, 1627, 201807, 6, 1642, 129335, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'GSP', '06-JUL-18 16:27:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 16:42:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Utility Company', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 3, 'S', 'YELLOW CREEK', 1, 'ESE', 'TAPOCO', 35.383, -83.876, 35.448, -83.941, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed across the North Carolina mountains and foothills during the afternoon and moved into the western Piedmont by early evening. A few of the storms produced strong to damaging winds that caused tree damage, with one tree  falling on a vehicle north of Lenoir, killing one of the occupants.', 'Dam operator reported multiple trees blown down along Highway 129 between Cheoah dam and Lake Santeetlah.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (775147, 201807, 6, 1230, 201807, 6, 1230, 129335, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'GSP', '06-JUL-18 12:30:00', 'EST-5', '06-JUL-18 12:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'ENE', 'CHIMNEY ROCK', 1, 'ENE', 'CHIMNEY ROCK', 35.437, -82.229, 35.437, -82.229, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed across the North Carolina mountains and foothills during the afternoon and moved into the western Piedmont by early evening. A few of the storms produced strong to damaging winds that caused tree damage, with one tree  falling on a vehicle north of Lenoir, killing one of the occupants.', 'County comms reported numerous trees blown down near Lake Lure.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (756166, 201807, 5, 1759, 201807, 5, 1800, 126135, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'JKL', '05-JUL-18 17:59:00', 'EST-5', '05-JUL-18 18:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Trained Spotter', 51, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'WNW', 'STANTON ARPT', 1, 'SSW', 'STANTON ARPT', 37.8539, -83.8586, 37.8416, -83.8547, 'Isolated to scattered strong to severe thunderstorms moved across portions of eastern Kentucky during the evening hours of July 5, 2018. The worst damage occurred in northeastern Frenchburg in Menifee County, where several hardwood trees were uprooted and a house had a portion of its metal roofing peeled back. London and Stanton also sustained wind damage as trees were blown down and hail up to the size of quarters fell.', 'A trained spotter and a local media outlet reported trees down from Maple Street in Stanton south to Mountain Parkway.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (754308, 201807, 1, 1815, 201807, 1, 1815, 125775, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'JKL', '01-JUL-18 18:15:00', 'EST-5', '01-JUL-18 18:15:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '911 Call Center', 51, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'NE', 'INEZ', 2, 'NE', 'INEZ', 37.8875, -82.5015, 37.8875, -82.5015, 'An isolated and slow moving severe thunderstorm moved across portions of Martin County on July 1st, 2018. The storm blew down numerous trees in the Turkey Creek area northeast of Inez, resulting in power outages.', 'Dispatch reported numerous trees were blown down in the Turkey Creek area of Kentucky Highway 908 northeast of Inez. As a result, several power outages occurred.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (756109, 201807, 4, 1810, 201807, 4, 1811, 126131, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'JKL', '04-JUL-18 18:10:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 18:11:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '60.00K', '0.00K', 'NWS Storm Survey', 74, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SW', 'PAINTSVILLE', 0, 'WSW', 'PAINTSVILLE', 37.8139, -82.8064, 37.8178, -82.8078, 'A cluster of strong to severe thunderstorms moved west/southwest from West Virginia into portions of northeast and east Kentucky this evening. Due to the high amount of moisture and subsequent instability in place, the downdraft portion of one of these storms produced winds of up to 85 mph as it collapsed over Paintsville. This resulted in substantial damage in Paintsville, including half of a roof being removed from an office building along with the steeple of a church being blown off. A couple of residential buildings were also damaged from falling trees.', 'An NWS Storm Survey confirmed microburst winds of between 75-85 mph removed half of a roof off of an office building and a steeple off of a church building in Paintsville. Several trees were also blown down, including one onto a residential building. A portion of Kentucky Highway 321/40 was shut down for a period of time due to downed and damaged trees.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760485, 201807, 4, 1630, 201807, 4, 1630, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 16:30:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 16:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'SW', 'GALLAGHER', 0, 'SW', 'GALLAGHER', 38.1677, -81.4043, 38.1677, -81.4043, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Several trees were blown down along Paint Creek Road near Gallagher.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760487, 201807, 4, 1632, 201807, 4, 1632, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 16:32:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 16:32:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NE', 'HERNSHAW', 1, 'NE', 'HERNSHAW', 38.2289, -81.5868, 38.2289, -81.5868, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'A couple trees were downed by the wind in the 2000-block of Lens Creek Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760489, 201807, 4, 1704, 201807, 4, 1704, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 17:04:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 17:04:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 45, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'SSE', 'GREENVIEW', 0, 'SSE', 'GREENVIEW', 37.9944, -81.8162, 37.9944, -81.8162, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'A tree was blown down near Greenview. After falling, it blocked part of Route 17.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760491, 201807, 4, 1742, 201807, 4, 1742, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 17:42:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 17:42:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'FETTERMAN', 1, 'SE', 'FETTERMAN', 39.3408, -80.016, 39.3408, -80.016, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Multiple trees were blown down near Grafton, some taking power lines down as well.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760492, 201807, 4, 1800, 201807, 4, 1800, 126499, 'WEST VIRGINIA', 54, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'RLX', '04-JUL-18 18:00:00', 'EST-5', '04-JUL-18 18:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'WSW', 'RIDER', 2, 'WSW', 'RIDER', 39.16, -80.4, 39.16, -80.4, 'Thunderstorms developed in a hot and humid airmass on the 4th, 5th and 6th. Some of these storms became severe, causing wind damage. One house was also struck by lightning. Minor flooding also resulted from slow storm movement.', 'Several trees, as well as a power line, were blown down along Duck Creek Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760061, 201807, 23, 430, 201807, 23, 430, 126794, 'FLORIDA', 12, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '23-JUL-18 04:30:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 04:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '100.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 60, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'E', 'BRADEN CASTLE', 1, 'E', 'BRADEN CASTLE', 27.5, -82.52, 27.5, -82.52, 'A strong outflow boundary moved south from the Florida Panhandle through the eastern Gulf of Mexico and onshore during the overnight and early morning hours of the 23rd. Numerous thunderstorms developed along the outflow, producing damaging wind gusts across west central Florida.', 'Significant wind damage was found in the Carlton Inlet Drive area of Bradenton. Sections of roof decking and shingles were removed from an apartment building, trees and branches were knocked down, and gutters, fascia and porch covers were damaged.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760059, 201807, 23, 420, 201807, 23, 420, 126794, 'FLORIDA', 12, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'TBW', '23-JUL-18 04:20:00', 'EST-5', '23-JUL-18 04:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '50.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 45, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'GILLETT', 1, 'W', 'GILLETT', 27.58, -82.54, 27.58, -82.54, 'A strong outflow boundary moved south from the Florida Panhandle through the eastern Gulf of Mexico and onshore during the overnight and early morning hours of the 23rd. Numerous thunderstorms developed along the outflow, producing damaging wind gusts across west central Florida.', 'Thunderstorm wind damage was reported at Coach House Mobile Home Park, with trees and power lines down and roof damage to mobile homes.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (794785, 201811, 13, 400, 201811, 13, 400, 132836, 'NORTH CAROLINA', 37, 2018, 'November', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'MHX', '13-NOV-18 04:00:00', 'EST-5', '13-NOV-18 04:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Public', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'SW', 'BUNYAN', 2, 'SW', 'BUNYAN', 35.51, -77, 35.51, -77, 'A supercell thunderstorm came ashore across Carteret County and produced a variety of severe weather. A waterspout formed offshore and came on land as a tornado. Severe thunderstorm winds also occurred in association with the same storm. Another severe thunderstorm produced wind damage in Beaufort County.', 'The public reported a swing set and gazebo was destroyed by the winds.  The location was near Washington off River Road.  This was relayed via social media.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763136, 201807, 27, 931, 201807, 27, 931, 127304, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '27-JUL-18 09:31:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 09:31:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Emergency Manager', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'S', 'MILLVILLE', 1, 'S', 'MILLVILLE', 39.3799, -75.0298, 39.3799, -75.0298, 'An approaching surface trough combined with moderate instability to produce widespread severe weather across the Mid-Atlantic. The event was well forecast with most of the area being highlighted in a Slight Risk Category by the Storm Prediction Center. Warm surface temperatures and dew points in the mid 70s lead to relatively high instability developed with forecast soundings suggesting 2000 J/kg CAPE values. An initial line of storms first developed over east-central Pennsylvania, then continued through the afternoon into the evening before storms congealed into several multi-cell clusters with several severe storms over New Jersey.', 'A tree was downed on NJ 47 north of Orange St. Time was best estimated from radar.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763135, 201807, 27, 1540, 201807, 27, 1540, 127304, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '27-JUL-18 15:40:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 15:40:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Social Media', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'WOODBRIDGE', 0, 'N', 'WOODBRIDGE', 40.57, -74.3, 40.57, -74.3, 'An approaching surface trough combined with moderate instability to produce widespread severe weather across the Mid-Atlantic. The event was well forecast with most of the area being highlighted in a Slight Risk Category by the Storm Prediction Center. Warm surface temperatures and dew points in the mid 70s lead to relatively high instability developed with forecast soundings suggesting 2000 J/kg CAPE values. An initial line of storms first developed over east-central Pennsylvania, then continued through the afternoon into the evening before storms congealed into several multi-cell clusters with several severe storms over New Jersey.', 'Numerous trees were downed in the area.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (790221, 201810, 2, 1738, 201810, 2, 1738, 129857, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'October', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'OKX', '02-OCT-18 17:38:00', 'EST-5', '02-OCT-18 17:38:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '3.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'NE', 'MT KISCO', 1, 'NE', 'MT KISCO', 41.2091, -73.7373, 41.2091, -73.7373, 'An approaching cold front triggered severe thunderstorms across southeastern New York, they produced 3 tornadoes across Rockland, Westchester and Suffolk Counties.', 'Trees down on Orchard Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763160, 201807, 27, 1334, 201807, 27, 1334, 127306, 'DELAWARE', 10, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '27-JUL-18 13:34:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 13:34:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Emergency Manager', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'DEWEY BEACH', 1, 'W', 'DEWEY BEACH', 38.6997, -75.08, 38.6997, -75.08, 'An approaching surface trough combined with moderate instability to produce widespread severe weather across the Mid-Atlantic. The event was well forecast with most of the area being highlighted in a Slight Risk Category by the Storm Prediction Center. Warm surface temperatures and dew points in the mid 70s lead to relatively high instability developed with forecast soundings suggesting 2000 J/kg CAPE values. An initial line of storms first developed over east-central Pennsylvania, then continued through the afternoon into the evening before storms congealed into several multi-cell clusters with several severe storms over New Jersey.', 'Utility poles and trees were downed near Dodd Ave. and Salisbury St. Roof damage to a home was also reported. Time best estimated from radar.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763173, 201807, 27, 1813, 201807, 27, 1813, 127307, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'PHI', '27-JUL-18 18:13:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 18:13:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Social Media', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'SCARLETS MILL', 1, 'W', 'SCARLETS MILL', 40.2302, -75.8693, 40.2302, -75.8693, 'An approaching surface trough combined with moderate instability to produce widespread severe weather across the Mid-Atlantic. The event was well forecast with most of the area being highlighted in a Slight Risk Category by the Storm Prediction Center. Warm surface temperatures and dew points in the mid 70s lead to relatively high instability developed with forecast soundings suggesting 2000 J/kg CAPE values. An initial line of storms first developed over east-central Pennsylvania, then continued through the afternoon into the evening before storms congealed into several multi-cell clusters with several severe storms over New Jersey.', 'Debris was reported to be covering Plow Rd. in Robeson Township from strong thunderstorm winds. Time best estimated from radar.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760683, 201807, 20, 1120, 201807, 20, 1120, 126919, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '20-JUL-18 11:20:00', 'EST-5', '20-JUL-18 11:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Other Federal Agency', 44, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 16, 'N', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 16, 'N', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 28.78, -80.8, 28.78, -80.8, 'Deep southwest flow was present across the Florida peninsula as a frontal trough was stalled across the Deep South and Western Atlantic, which was keeping the axis of the Bermuda Ridge pinned across the Florida Straits. Abundant moisture was present across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Strong diurnal heating resulted in numerous showers and thunderstorms across inland areas, which were pushed towards the east coast by the dominant southwest steering flow. These storms moved over the intracoastal waters of Brevard County where they produced strong winds.', 'U.S. Air Force wind tower 0421 measured a peak wind gust of 44 knots from the west.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760684, 201807, 20, 1125, 201807, 20, 1125, 126919, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '20-JUL-18 11:25:00', 'EST-5', '20-JUL-18 11:25:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Other Federal Agency', 40, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 17, 'N', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 17, 'N', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 28.8, -80.74, 28.8, -80.74, 'Deep southwest flow was present across the Florida peninsula as a frontal trough was stalled across the Deep South and Western Atlantic, which was keeping the axis of the Bermuda Ridge pinned across the Florida Straits. Abundant moisture was present across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Strong diurnal heating resulted in numerous showers and thunderstorms across inland areas, which were pushed towards the east coast by the dominant southwest steering flow. These storms moved over the intracoastal waters of Brevard County where they produced strong winds.', 'U.S. Air Force wind tower 0022 measured a peak wind gust of 40 knots from the west-southwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760736, 201807, 21, 1420, 201807, 21, 1420, 126921, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '21-JUL-18 14:20:00', 'EST-5', '21-JUL-18 14:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Buoy', 37, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'BUOY 41009', 0, 'N', 'BUOY 41009', 28.52, -80.17, 28.52, -80.17, 'An anomalous surface trough was draped across the deep south, with a weak embedded low pressure center located along the Carolina coast. This feature was supported by mid to upper level troughing that produced deep layer west to southwest flow across the Florida peninsula. This pattern favored showers and thunderstorms developing along the west coast sea breeze and outflow boundaries, and negated formation of the east coast sea breeze. Ample moisture and daytime heating allowed showers and storms to develop early in the morning and move across the area. As storms moved across Brevard County coast they produced many reports of strong wind gusts.', 'Buoy 41009 measured a peak wind gust of 37 knots from the west-southwest.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (760685, 201807, 20, 1130, 201807, 20, 1130, 126919, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '20-JUL-18 11:30:00', 'EST-5', '20-JUL-18 11:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Other Federal Agency', 37, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 14, 'NNE', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 14, 'NNE', 'PLAYALINDA BEACH', 28.74, -80.7, 28.74, -80.7, 'Deep southwest flow was present across the Florida peninsula as a frontal trough was stalled across the Deep South and Western Atlantic, which was keeping the axis of the Bermuda Ridge pinned across the Florida Straits. Abundant moisture was present across the area with high Precipitable Water values. Strong diurnal heating resulted in numerous showers and thunderstorms across inland areas, which were pushed towards the east coast by the dominant southwest steering flow. These storms moved over the intracoastal waters of Brevard County where they produced strong winds.', 'U.S. Air Force wind tower 0019 measured a peak wind gust of 37 knots from the west.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763463, 201807, 22, 1608, 201807, 22, 1608, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 16:08:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 16:08:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'ASOS', 36, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 12, 'E', 'VERO BEACH', 12, 'E', 'VERO BEACH', 27.656, -80.376, 27.656, -80.376, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'The ASOS at the Vero Beach Airport (KVRB) measured a peak wind gust of 36 knots from the north.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (763464, 201807, 22, 1634, 201807, 22, 1634, 127194, 'ATLANTIC SOUTH', 87, 2018, 'July', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'MLB', '22-JUL-18 16:34:00', 'EST-5', '22-JUL-18 16:34:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Mesonet', 35, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'ESE', 'ST. LUCIE NUCLEAR POWER PLANT', 1, 'ESE', 'ST. LUCIE NUCLEAR POWER PLANT', 27.3452, -80.2364, 27.3452, -80.2364, 'A large mid-to-upper-level low pressure system centered over Ohio was expanding southward across the southeastern United States. As this occurred, a series of strong disturbances aloft traveled across the Florida peninsula. Environmental conditions supported numerous strong thunderstorms due to favorable vertical lift, wind shear and a very moist atmosphere. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms developed during the afternoon and evening across northeast Florida. Over time these storms merged into a strong to severe Mesoscale Convective System (MCS) that moved south across east central Florida. Other storms also developed along the local sea breezes, and residual outflow boundaries. As the MCS moved across the intracoastal and nearshore waters of east central Florida, numerous strong wind events occurred from Volusia County south to St. Lucie County. This episode continued into the early morning hours of Monday (July 23) as a second, weaker MCS moved across the area from north to south, bringing strong winds to the Brevard County coast.', 'A Weatherflow site at the St. Lucie Nuclear Power Plant (XSTL) measured a peak wind gust of 35 knots from the west.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (782489, 201809, 25, 2330, 201809, 26, 930, 130764, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'RLX', '25-SEP-18 23:30:00', 'EST-5', '26-SEP-18 09:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'E', 'MARIETTA', 2, 'SW', 'WARNER', 39.4199, -81.433, 39.5492, -81.4446, 'On the 23rd a surface boundary was stalled across southern West Virginia. It slowly moved north as a warm front on the 24th and 25th as a surface low crossed the region. This low then pushed a cold front through on the 26th and 27th. Atmospheric moisture was anomalously high throughout the period, leading to multiple rounds of moderate to heavy rain which caused some flooding.', 'The stream gage on Duck Creek near Whipple showed the creek rose above its 12 foot flood stage late on the 25th. The creek crested at 12.4 feet just before sunrise on the 26th and had returned to its banks by mid morning. This flooded sections of State Routes 26, 145 and 821.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (782496, 201809, 25, 1900, 201809, 26, 800, 130764, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'RLX', '25-SEP-18 19:00:00', 'EST-5', '26-SEP-18 08:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.50K', '0.00K', 'River/Stream Gage', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 0, 'SW', 'BLOOMFIELD', 2, 'NE', 'FIFTEEN', 39.5652, -81.2056, 39.5468, -81.2602, 'On the 23rd a surface boundary was stalled across southern West Virginia. It slowly moved north as a warm front on the 24th and 25th as a surface low crossed the region. This low then pushed a cold front through on the 26th and 27th. Atmospheric moisture was anomalously high throughout the period, leading to multiple rounds of moderate to heavy rain which caused some flooding.', 'The Little Muskingum River flooded, closing Route 26 near its intersection with Route 260. The stream gage near Bloomfield showed the river rose above its 16 foot flood stage on the evening of the 25th. It crested in minor flood, around 18.5 feet after midnight and returned to its banks shortly after sunrise on the 26th.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (790220, 201810, 2, 1545, 201810, 2, 1545, 129857, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'October', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'OKX', '02-OCT-18 15:45:00', 'EST-5', '02-OCT-18 15:45:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '3.00K', '0.00K', 'Department of Highways', 52, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SSW', 'CROTON HGTS', 1, 'SSW', 'CROTON HGTS', 41.2393, -73.8041, 41.2393, -73.8041, 'An approaching cold front triggered severe thunderstorms across southeastern New York, they produced 3 tornadoes across Rockland, Westchester and Suffolk Counties.', 'NY 129 between NY 118 and Underhill Avenue closed due to downed tree and wires.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771672, 201807, 27, 1551, 201807, 27, 1551, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 15:51:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 15:51:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Public', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 2, 'W', 'GLENFORD', 2, 'W', 'GLENFORD', 42, -74.15, 42, -74.15, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'Trees and limbs were downed along Route 28 between West Hurley and Shokan.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771673, 201807, 27, 1553, 201807, 27, 1553, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 15:53:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 15:53:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 4, 'W', 'BREAKABEEN', 4, 'W', 'BREAKABEEN', 42.52, -74.5, 42.52, -74.5, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'A tree was downed across the road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (771676, 201807, 27, 1630, 201807, 27, 1630, 128650, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'ALY', '27-JUL-18 16:30:00', 'EST-5', '27-JUL-18 16:30:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Trained Spotter', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'COXSACKIE', 1, 'W', 'COXSACKIE', 42.35, -73.81, 42.35, -73.81, 'Scattered thunderstorms developed ahead of a slow-moving cold front during the afternoon and evening of July 27th. The first cluster of storms that developed in the early afternoon produced fairly extensive wind damage over portions of the Capital District in addition to hail up to golf ball size. The wind brought down several large trees onto houses in and around Albany and Troy and damaged an outdoor stage set up on a golf course. Several gravestones were shattered in Albany Rural Cemetery when trees fell on them. More than 5,000 households lost power in Albany County and some were without power for up to 36 hours.||Additional strong to severe storms affected portions of the Catskills, Schoharie and Mohawk Valleys, and Mid Hudson Valley during the afternoon and evening with isolated wind damage.', 'A large tree, large tree limbs, and power lines were downed.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (776155, 201809, 24, 1700, 201809, 24, 1800, 129544, 'KENTUCKY', 21, 2018, 'September', 'Flood', 'ILN', '24-SEP-18 17:00:00', 'EST-5', '24-SEP-18 18:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'State Official', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'W', 'HELENA', 2, 'WSW', 'HELENA', 38.4972, -83.7969, 38.4939, -83.797, 'Showers and thunderstorms developed along a stationary boundary located across the Ohio Valley. A few of storms produced locally heavy rainfall.', 'High water was reported on Helena Road.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786549, 201809, 21, 1656, 201809, 21, 1656, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 16:56:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 16:56:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '10.00K', '0.00K', 'Law Enforcement', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'EAST AURORA', 1, 'W', 'EAST AURORA', 42.77, -78.62, 42.77, -78.62, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'A tree fell on a house on Girard Avenue.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786550, 201809, 21, 1702, 201809, 21, 1702, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 17:02:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 17:02:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'ELLINGTON', 0, 'N', 'ELLINGTON', 42.22, -79.1, 42.22, -79.1, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'Trees were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786551, 201809, 21, 1716, 201809, 21, 1716, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 17:16:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 17:16:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'LITTLE VLY', 1, 'W', 'LITTLE VLY', 42.25, -78.8, 42.25, -78.8, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'Trees and wires were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (750569, 201804, 19, 1224, 201804, 19, 1242, 125157, 'ATLANTIC NORTH', 88, 2018, 'April', 'Marine Thunderstorm Wind', 'LWX', '19-APR-18 12:24:00', 'EST-5', '19-APR-18 12:42:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Buoy', 36, 'MG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'LEWISETTA (LWS)', 0, 'N', 'LEWISETTA (LWS)', 38, -76.47, 38, -76.47, 'A strong cold front passed through, and showers were able to mix down gusty winds from aloft.', 'Wind gusts up to 36 knots were reported at Lewisetta.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (786552, 201809, 21, 1720, 201809, 21, 1720, 131456, 'NEW YORK', 36, 2018, 'September', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'BUF', '21-SEP-18 17:20:00', 'EST-5', '21-SEP-18 17:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2.00K', '0.00K', '911 Call Center', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SE', 'JAVA CENTER', 1, 'SE', 'JAVA CENTER', 42.64, -78.39, 42.64, -78.39, 'An unusually strong wind field was in place ahead of a well defined cold front. This supported very high effective bulk shear values along with very high levels of helicity. All of this supported cells that quickly formed into a textbook line echo wave pattern (LEWP) which quickly moved across the area. There were a handful of spin ups within the LEWP that developed very deep mesocyclones with persistent wind threats.', 'Trees and wires were reported down.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (773183, 201807, 26, 1755, 201807, 26, 1755, 128939, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '26-JUL-18 17:55:00', 'EST-5', '26-JUL-18 17:55:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'COOP Observer', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'S', 'SHADELAND', 0, 'S', 'SHADELAND', 41.8156, -80.3794, 41.8156, -80.3794, 'A cold front swept east across the Upper Ohio Valley on July 26th causing a line of thunderstorms to develop. Some storm damage was reported in Erie and Crawford Counties.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed a tree along Shadeland Road just west of State Route 18.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (773184, 201807, 26, 1814, 201807, 26, 1814, 128939, 'PENNSYLVANIA', 42, 2018, 'July', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'CLE', '26-JUL-18 18:14:00', 'EST-5', '26-JUL-18 18:14:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '5.00K', '0.00K', 'Broadcast Media', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'EDINBORO', 0, 'N', 'EDINBORO', 41.87, -80.13, 41.87, -80.13, 'A cold front swept east across the Upper Ohio Valley on July 26th causing a line of thunderstorms to develop. Some storm damage was reported in Erie and Crawford Counties.', 'Thunderstorm winds downed some trees in the Edinboro area.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (743497, 201803, 19, 2255, 201803, 19, 2305, 123500, 'GEORGIA', 13, 2018, 'March', 'Thunderstorm Wind', 'FFC', '19-MAR-18 22:55:00', 'EST-5', '19-MAR-18 23:05:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '4.00K', NULL, 'Emergency Manager', 50, 'EG', NULL, NULL, 1, 'SSE', 'MARBLE VALLEY', 1, 'SSE', 'MARBLE VALLEY', 33.6099, -83.8766, 33.6099, -83.8766, 'Widespread severe thunderstorms broke out across central and north Georgia during the evening hours of March 19th, through the early morning hours of the 20th as a warm front lifted north across the region ahead of a strong storm system developing across the lower Mississippi Valley.', 'The Newton County Emergency Manager reported a large tree and power lines blown down on Geiger Street near the county Emergency Services Office.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (773193, 201807, 31, 2150, 201807, 31, 2200, 128941, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Tornado', 'CLE', '31-JUL-18 21:50:00', 'EST-5', '31-JUL-18 22:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '150.00K', '0.00K', 'Emergency Manager', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 'WSW', 'BOOTH', 0, 'E', 'PT PLACE', 41.6219, -83.4714, 41.7201, -83.4714, 'A weak area of low pressure moved north across Ohio late on July 31st.  Some scattered showers and a few thunderstorms developed in advance of the low.  A brief tornado was reported over Marion County and a second tornado occurred in Lucas County.  Damage from the Marion County tornado was minimal but some homes were damaged in Lucas County.', 'A tornado touched down near Oregon and tracked due north to near Point Place before dissipating.  The nearly seven mile long damage patch was intermittent and consisted of mainly tree damage.  Some homes sustained roof damage, mainly from lost shingles.  A barn along the damage path did sustain significant wind damage.  A video of a SUV being lifted and spun suggests the tornado was at least a high end EF1 in intensity at its peak.  A couple other vehicles in the area were displaced.  The tornado had a maximum width of around 25 yards.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (773237, 201807, 31, 2136, 201807, 31, 2138, 128941, 'OHIO', 39, 2018, 'July', 'Tornado', 'CLE', '31-JUL-18 21:36:00', 'EST-5', '31-JUL-18 21:38:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '25.00K', '0.00K', 'Trained Spotter', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, 'ESE', 'OWENS', 2, 'E', 'OWENS', 40.513, -83.1153, 40.5201, -83.1082, 'A weak area of low pressure moved north across Ohio late on July 31st.  Some scattered showers and a few thunderstorms developed in advance of the low.  A brief tornado was reported over Marion County and a second tornado occurred in Lucas County.  Damage from the Marion County tornado was minimal but some homes were damaged in Lucas County.', 'An EF0 tornado touched down in a corn field along Benzler Lust Road just to the east of Benzler Road.  The tornado tracked northeast for just over a half mile and lifted as it approached Owens Road.  A barn near the initial touchdown lost its roof and a tree was knocked down nearby.  Some crop damage also occurred.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (733987, 201801, 12, 1536, 201801, 13, 1100, 122478, 'CONNECTICUT', 9, 2018, 'January', 'Flood', 'BOX', '12-JAN-18 15:36:00', 'EST-5', '13-JAN-18 11:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Amateur Radio', NULL, NULL, 'Heavy Rain', NULL, 1, 'NW', 'NEWINGTON', 1, 'NW', 'NEWINGTON', 41.6931, -72.7327, 41.6933, -72.7321, 'A slow-moving cold front crossed New England from the afternoon of January 12 to the morning of January 13. Strong southerly winds ahead of the front drew mild and humid air north over Southern New England. This helped generate heavy downpours before the front moved through.  Rainfall amounts ranged from one to three inches, except in Southeast Massachusetts where amounts ranged up to four inches.  Maximum wind gusts ranged from 45 to 65 mph.', 'At 336 PM EST in Newington, Willard Avenue at Garfield Street was reported closed due to flooding. Rainfall between 1.5 inches and 3.0 inches was reported in Hartford County.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (734039, 201803, 7, 1435, 201803, 7, 1435, 122553, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'March', 'Lightning', 'PHI', '07-MAR-18 14:35:00', 'EST-5', '07-MAR-18 14:35:00', 1, 0, 0, 0, '0.00K', '0.00K', 'Trained Spotter', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'W', 'WHITING', 1, 'W', 'WHITING', 39.95, -74.4, 39.95, -74.4, 'A broad area of low pressure extending from the Ohio Valley to the Piedmont of South Carolina consolidated off the Virginia Capes during the early morning of March 7th. This new primary low moved northeast and gradually deepened as it passed east of the Delaware and New Jersey coasts on March 7th.||Precipitation gradually overspread the region during the overnight hours of March 6th to the 7th. To the east of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95, precipitation began as rain or a mix of rain and snow. Further west, precipitation fell mainly as snow. During the daylight hours of the 7th, precipitation to the east of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95 turned over to snow, as colder air worked in from the north and west. ||The snow fell heavy at times away from the coast.  Snowfall amounts near the Turnpike generally ranged from 6 to 12 inches, with a sharp decrease to the southeast. Further northwest, 12 to 24 inches was observed across large parts of Somerset, Hunterdon, Morris, and Sussex Counties.||The snow contained large amounts of liquid, making it heavy and wet. This resulted in downed trees, limbs, and wires, leading to numerous power outages across portions of New Jersey, especially where the heaviest snow was reported. Many customers were still without power from the previous storm when this storm struck. Governor Murphy estimated about 350,000 customers state-wide lost power as a result of this second storm.||There were numerous reports of lightning associated with the precipitation in New Jersey, mainly southeast of the Turnpike. This included thunderstorms with heavy rainfall closer to the coast, and thunder with heavy snowfall further inland. In Ocean County, a person was struck by lightning in Manchester Township, and a lightning strike led to a house fire in Ship Bottom.||Governor Phil Murphy declared a state of emergency which went into effect at 8 PM Tuesday March 6th.||Flights were cancelled at all the major airports due to the storm, and Amtrak cancelled at least some Wednesday service.||An accident involving ten tractor-trailers closed all four lanes of the New Jersey bound span of the Delaware Memorial Bridge for over two hours on Wednesday, March 7th.  Large amounts of snow that accumulated in a short period of time was blamed for the crash. The trucks did not actually crash into each other, rather they got stuck in the snow as they were climbing the ramp on the east-bound bridge.||Minor flooding was reported along some portions of the New Jersey coast, particularly north of Atlantic City, but there were no major problems.', 'A broad area of low pressure extending from the Ohio Valley to the Piedmont of South Carolina consolidated off the Virginia Capes during the early morning of March 7th. This new, primary low moved Northeast and gradually deepened as it moved East of the Delaware and New Jersey Coasts on March 7th.||Precipitation gradually overspread the region during the overnight hours of March 6th to the 7th. To the East of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95, precipitation began as rain or a mix of rain and snow. Further West, precipitation fell mainly as snow. During the daylight hours of the 7th, precipitation to the East of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95 turned over to snow, as colder air worked in from the North and West.||The snow fell heavy at times West of the New Jersey Coast. Snowfall amounts near the Turnpike generally ranged from 6 to 12 inches, with a sharp decrease to the Southeast. Further Northwest, 12 to 24 inches was observed across large parts of Somerset, Hunterdon, Morris, and Sussex Counties.||The snow contained large amounts of liquid, making it heavy and wet. This resulted in trees, limbs, and wires down, leading to numerous power outages across portions of New Jersey.||There were numerous reports of lightning associated with the precipitation in New Jersey, mainly to the Southeast of the Turnpike. This included thunderstorms with heavy rainfall closer to the coast, and thunder with heavy snowfall further inland. In Ocean County New Jersey, a person was struck by lightning at the middle school in Manchester Township.');
INSERT INTO public.stormevents_east VALUES (734040, 201803, 7, 1420, 201803, 7, 1420, 122553, 'NEW JERSEY', 34, 2018, 'March', 'Lightning', 'PHI', '07-MAR-18 14:20:00', 'EST-5', '07-MAR-18 14:20:00', 0, 0, 0, 0, '1.00K', '0.00K', 'Newspaper', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'N', 'LAKEWOOD', 0, 'N', 'LAKEWOOD', 40.1, -74.22, 40.1, -74.22, 'A broad area of low pressure extending from the Ohio Valley to the Piedmont of South Carolina consolidated off the Virginia Capes during the early morning of March 7th. This new primary low moved northeast and gradually deepened as it passed east of the Delaware and New Jersey coasts on March 7th.||Precipitation gradually overspread the region during the overnight hours of March 6th to the 7th. To the east of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95, precipitation began as rain or a mix of rain and snow. Further west, precipitation fell mainly as snow. During the daylight hours of the 7th, precipitation to the east of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95 turned over to snow, as colder air worked in from the north and west. ||The snow fell heavy at times away from the coast.  Snowfall amounts near the Turnpike generally ranged from 6 to 12 inches, with a sharp decrease to the southeast. Further northwest, 12 to 24 inches was observed across large parts of Somerset, Hunterdon, Morris, and Sussex Counties.||The snow contained large amounts of liquid, making it heavy and wet. This resulted in downed trees, limbs, and wires, leading to numerous power outages across portions of New Jersey, especially where the heaviest snow was reported. Many customers were still without power from the previous storm when this storm struck. Governor Murphy estimated about 350,000 customers state-wide lost power as a result of this second storm.||There were numerous reports of lightning associated with the precipitation in New Jersey, mainly southeast of the Turnpike. This included thunderstorms with heavy rainfall closer to the coast, and thunder with heavy snowfall further inland. In Ocean County, a person was struck by lightning in Manchester Township, and a lightning strike led to a house fire in Ship Bottom.||Governor Phil Murphy declared a state of emergency which went into effect at 8 PM Tuesday March 6th.||Flights were cancelled at all the major airports due to the storm, and Amtrak cancelled at least some Wednesday service.||An accident involving ten tractor-trailers closed all four lanes of the New Jersey bound span of the Delaware Memorial Bridge for over two hours on Wednesday, March 7th.  Large amounts of snow that accumulated in a short period of time was blamed for the crash. The trucks did not actually crash into each other, rather they got stuck in the snow as they were climbing the ramp on the east-bound bridge.||Minor flooding was reported along some portions of the New Jersey coast, particularly north of Atlantic City, but there were no major problems.', 'A broad area of low pressure extending from the Ohio Valley to the Piedmont of South Carolina consolidated off the Virginia Capes during the early morning of March 7th. This new, primary low moved Northeast and gradually deepened as it moved East of the Delaware and New Jersey Coasts on March 7th.||Precipitation gradually overspread the region during the overnight hours of March 6th to the 7th. To the East of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95, precipitation began as rain or a mix of rain and snow. Further West, precipitation fell mainly as snow. During the daylight hours of the 7th, precipitation to the East of the NJ Turnpike/Interstate 95 turned over to snow, as colder air worked in from the North and West.||The snow fell heavy at times West of the New Jersey Coast. Snowfall amounts near the Turnpike generally ranged from 6 to 12 inches, with a sharp decrease to the Southeast. Further Northwest, 12 to 24 inches was observed across large parts of Somerset, Hunterdon, Morris, and Sussex Counties.||The snow contained large amounts of liquid, making it heavy and wet. This resulted in trees, limbs, and wires down, leading to numerous power outages across portions of New Jersey.||There were numerous reports of lightning associated with the precipitation in New Jersey, mainly to the Southeast of the Turnpike. This included thunderstorms with heavy rainfall closer to the coast, and thunder with heavy snowfall further inland. In Ocean County New Jersey, a lightning strike lead to a structure fire in Lakewood.');
